window.REV_FLIP=window.REV_FLIP||{};window.REV_FLIP["database-with-python"]=[{"id":"database-with-python-f0001","card":"q-database-with-python-041-mysql-database-management","sec":"database-with-python-s042","q":"What happens when you drop a database?","a":"<p>The data is lost for good, so back it up first.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0002","card":"q-database-with-python-042-mysql-table-management","sec":"database-with-python-s043","q":"Which constraints should you know?","a":"<p>PRIMARY KEY, FOREIGN KEY, UNIQUE and NOT NULL, plus the CASCADE options on foreign keys.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0003","card":"q-database-with-python-043-mysql-data-manipulation-dml","sec":"database-with-python-s044","q":"DELETE vs TRUNCATE?","a":"<p>DELETE removes specific rows (with a WHERE clause). TRUNCATE empties the whole table and resets it. Always use WHERE when you update or delete.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0004","card":"q-database-with-python-045-mysql-joins-subqueries-union-and-case","sec":"database-with-python-s046","q":"INNER vs OUTER join?","a":"<p>INNER keeps only rows that match in both tables. LEFT and RIGHT outer joins also keep unmatched rows from one side. Be ready to write queries with several joins, subqueries and aggregations.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0005","card":"q-database-with-python-046-mysql-indexing","sec":"database-with-python-s047","q":"When do you add an index and what does it cost?","a":"<p>Index columns that are queried often. The cost is slower INSERT and UPDATE operations.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0006","card":"q-database-with-python-047-mysql-users-and-privileges","sec":"database-with-python-s048","q":"How do you secure access?","a":"<p>Know the privilege levels (global, database, table) and grant the minimum needed.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0007","card":"q-database-with-python-048-mysql-transactions","sec":"database-with-python-s049","q":"What are the ACID properties and when do you need transactions?","a":"<p>Atomicity, Consistency, Isolation, Durability. Use transactions for work that must succeed or fail together, such as financial operations.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0008","card":"q-database-with-python-049-mysql-views","sec":"database-with-python-s050","q":"Why use views?","a":"<p>They abstract complex queries and add a security layer. A limitation is that they are not always updatable.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0009","card":"q-database-with-python-050-mysql-stored-procedures-and-functions","sec":"database-with-python-s051","q":"Procedure vs function?","a":"<p>Use stored procedures for complex logic and security. Use functions for reusable calculations you can call inside a query.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0010","card":"q-database-with-python-051-mysql-triggers","sec":"database-with-python-s052","q":"What are triggers for and what do they cost?","a":"<p>Logging and enforcing rules. They add performance overhead.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0011","card":"q-database-with-python-052-mysql-performance-tuning-commands","sec":"database-with-python-s053","q":"How do you optimize MySQL performance?","a":"<p>Indexing strategy, query optimization (avoid <code>SELECT *</code>), and caching (the InnoDB buffer pool).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0012","card":"q-database-with-python-053-mysql-backup-restore-and-server-variable","sec":"database-with-python-s054","q":"Logical vs physical backups?","a":"<p><code>mysqldump</code> is a logical backup. A physical backup copies the data files. Also know point-in-time recovery. Key variables: <code>innodb_buffer_pool_size</code>, <code>max_connections</code>, <code>query_cache_size</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0013","card":"q-database-with-python-054-mysql-partitioning-events-and-full-text","sec":"database-with-python-s055","q":"What partitioning types exist and when is full-text search better than a normal index?","a":"<p>RANGE, LIST and HASH. Full-text indexes serve word search over text, which a regular index cannot do well.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0014","card":"q-database-with-python-055-mysql-common-interview-queries","sec":"database-with-python-s056","q":"How do you normalize a table?","a":"<p>Break a denormalized table into 1NF, 2NF and 3NF. <strong>Q. How do you handle deadlocks?</strong> Detect them with <code>SHOW ENGINE INNODB STATUS</code> and prevent them with a consistent locking order.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0015","card":"q-database-with-python-057-mysql-storage-engines","sec":"database-with-python-s058","q":"InnoDB vs MyISAM?","a":"<p>InnoDB is transactional with row-level locking. MyISAM is non-transactional with table-level locking.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0016","card":"q-database-with-python-058-mysql-replication-and-high-availability","sec":"database-with-python-s059","q":"How does replication help?","a":"<p>A primary-replica setup scales reads (read/write splitting). Be ready to discuss replication lag.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0017","card":"q-database-with-python-059-mysql-recursive-ctes-and-advanced-window","sec":"database-with-python-s060","q":"When do you use a recursive CTE?","a":"<p>For tree-like data such as employee-manager relationships. Learn <code>RANK()</code>, <code>DENSE_RANK()</code>, <code>ROW_NUMBER()</code> and aggregate window functions.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0018","card":"q-database-with-python-060-mysql-large-datasets-stored-procedure-er","sec":"database-with-python-s061","q":"How do you manage very large tables?","a":"<p>Delete in batches, and use partitioning or archiving. <strong>Q. How do you harden MySQL?</strong> Remove anonymous users, disable remote root login, use SSL, and handle errors in stored procedures so production failures roll back cleanly.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0019","card":"q-database-with-python-061-mysql-json-profiling-and-scaling","sec":"database-with-python-s062","q":"When do you use JSON columns?","a":"<p>For flexible schemas. Use profiling and the slow query log to find slow queries. <strong>Q. How does MySQL scale out?</strong> MySQL Cluster (NDB) or sharding, which has challenges such as data distribution. There is no single command for it.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0020","card":"q-database-with-python-062-postgresql-databases-and-schemas","sec":"database-with-python-s063","q":"Why use schemas?","a":"<p>They organize objects and help multi-tenant applications. Know the database creation options (ENCODING, TEMPLATE) and connection management.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0021","card":"q-database-with-python-065-postgresql-indexes","sec":"database-with-python-s066","q":"B-tree vs GIN?","a":"<p>B-tree is the default for equality and range lookups. GIN suits JSONB and full-text data. Both affect performance.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0022","card":"q-database-with-python-067-postgresql-transactions-and-isolation","sec":"database-with-python-s068","q":"What are the isolation levels?","a":"<p>Compare READ COMMITTED, REPEATABLE READ and SERIALIZABLE and their trade-offs, and explain ACID.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0023","card":"q-database-with-python-068-postgresql-views-and-materialized-views","sec":"database-with-python-s069","q":"View vs materialized view?","a":"<p>A view is computed dynamically on each query. A materialized view stores (caches) the result until you refresh it.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0024","card":"q-database-with-python-071-postgresql-recursive-ctes-replication-an","sec":"database-with-python-s072","q":"Streaming vs logical replication?","a":"<p>Be able to explain both. Popular extensions include PostGIS and UUID-OSSP.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0025","card":"q-database-with-python-072-postgresql-interview-queries","sec":"database-with-python-s073","q":"PostgreSQL vs MySQL talking points?","a":"<p>JSONB, window functions and extensibility. Also be ready to explain MVCC (Multiversion Concurrency Control), handle NULLs, and optimize slow queries. For DBA roles stress replication, vacuuming and configuration tuning. For developer roles stress complex queries and JSONB. Practise 20 to 30 SQL problems on LeetCode or HackerRank, and test commands on a local instance (Docker works).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0026","card":"q-database-with-python-073-postgresql-partial-and-expression-indexe","sec":"database-with-python-s074","q":"When do these help?","a":"<p>Partial indexes cover only the rows you filter on. Expression indexes support queries such as case-insensitive search.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0027","card":"q-database-with-python-075-postgresql-error-handling-and-full-text","sec":"database-with-python-s076","q":"Full-text search vs LIKE?","a":"<p>Full-text search with a GIN index is faster and understands words, while <code>LIKE</code> scans text.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0028","card":"q-database-with-python-078-python-basics-what-it-is-and-how-it-runs","sec":"database-with-python-s079","q":"What is Python, and what are its key features?","a":"<p>A high-level, interpreted language known for simplicity. Features: readable syntax, dynamic typing, extensive libraries, cross-platform, multi-paradigm (procedural, OOP, functional), garbage-collected.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0029","card":"q-database-with-python-078-python-basics-what-it-is-and-how-it-runs","sec":"database-with-python-s079","q":"Python 2 vs Python 3?","a":"<p>Python 2 reached end of life in 2020. In Python 3, <code>print</code> is a function, <code>5/2</code> gives <code>2.5</code> (float division), Unicode is native, <code>range()</code> replaces <code>xrange()</code>, and modern features such as f-strings exist.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0030","card":"q-database-with-python-078-python-basics-what-it-is-and-how-it-runs","sec":"database-with-python-s079","q":"What are PEP 8 guidelines and why do they matter?","a":"<p>Python's style guide: 4-space indentation, 79-character lines, snake_case for functions. It keeps code readable and consistent for collaboration.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0031","card":"q-database-with-python-078-python-basics-what-it-is-and-how-it-runs","sec":"database-with-python-s079","q":"How is Python an interpreted language?","a":"<p>The interpreter runs code line by line, converting it to bytecode that the Python Virtual Machine (PVM) executes. It is not compiled to machine code.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0032","card":"q-database-with-python-078-python-basics-what-it-is-and-how-it-runs","sec":"database-with-python-s079","q":"How does Python handle memory management?","a":"<p>Reference counting (memory is freed when the count hits 0) plus a garbage collector for cyclic references, available through the <code>gc</code> module.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0033","card":"q-database-with-python-079-python-data-types-and-mutability","sec":"database-with-python-s080","q":"Lists vs tuples vs sets?","a":"<p>Lists <code>[1, 2]</code> are mutable, ordered, and allow duplicates. Tuples <code>(1, 2)</code> are immutable, ordered, and allow duplicates. Sets <code>{1, 2}</code> are mutable, unordered, and have no duplicates.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0034","card":"q-database-with-python-079-python-data-types-and-mutability","sec":"database-with-python-s080","q":"<code>==</code> vs <code>is</code>?","a":"<p><code>==</code> checks value equality. <code>is</code> checks identity (same memory location).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>a = [1, 2]; b = [1, 2]\nprint(a == b)  # True\nprint(a is b)  # False</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0035","card":"q-database-with-python-079-python-data-types-and-mutability","sec":"database-with-python-s080","q":"Mutable vs immutable objects?","a":"<p>Mutable: lists, dicts, sets. Immutable: int, str, tuple.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0036","card":"q-database-with-python-079-python-data-types-and-mutability","sec":"database-with-python-s080","q":"What are Python's built-in data types?","a":"<p>Numeric (<code>int</code>, <code>float</code>, <code>complex</code>), sequence (<code>str</code>, <code>list</code>, <code>tuple</code>), mapping (<code>dict</code>), set (<code>set</code>, <code>frozenset</code>), boolean (<code>bool</code>), and <code>None</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0037","card":"q-database-with-python-079-python-data-types-and-mutability","sec":"database-with-python-s080","q":"<code>range()</code> vs <code>xrange()</code>?","a":"<p>In Python 2, <code>range()</code> returns a list and <code>xrange()</code> an iterator. In Python 3 only <code>range()</code> exists and it behaves like <code>xrange()</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0038","card":"q-database-with-python-080-python-basics-statements-and-arguments","sec":"database-with-python-s081","q":"What does <code>pass</code> do?","a":"<p>It is a no-op placeholder for an empty code block.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def func(): pass</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0039","card":"q-database-with-python-080-python-basics-statements-and-arguments","sec":"database-with-python-s081","q":"How do you swap two variables without a temp variable?","a":"<p>Tuple unpacking.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>a, b = 5, 10; a, b = b, a  # a=10, b=5</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0040","card":"q-database-with-python-080-python-basics-statements-and-arguments","sec":"database-with-python-s081","q":"What is a module and how do you import one?","a":"<p>A file of reusable code.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import math; print(math.sqrt(16))  # 4.0</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0041","card":"q-database-with-python-080-python-basics-statements-and-arguments","sec":"database-with-python-s081","q":"What does <code>if __name__ == \"__main__\":</code> do?","a":"<p>It runs the code only when the script is executed directly, not when imported.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    print(&quot;Direct run&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0042","card":"q-database-with-python-080-python-basics-statements-and-arguments","sec":"database-with-python-s081","q":"What are <code>*args</code> and `","a":"<p>kwargs<code>?** </code>*args<code>collects variable positional arguments (a tuple).</code>**kwargs` collects variable keyword arguments (a dict).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def func(*args, **kwargs):\n    print(args, kwargs)\nfunc(1, 2, a=3)  # (1, 2) {&#x27;a&#x27;: 3}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0043","card":"q-database-with-python-081-strings-reverse-slice-palindrome","sec":"database-with-python-s082","q":"How do you reverse a string?","a":"<p>Slice with a step of -1.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>s = &quot;hello&quot;; print(s[::-1])  # &quot;olleh&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0044","card":"q-database-with-python-081-strings-reverse-slice-palindrome","sec":"database-with-python-s082","q":"How does string slicing work?","a":"<p><code>[start:stop:step]</code> extracts a substring.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>s = &quot;Python&quot;; print(s[1:4])  # &quot;yth&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0045","card":"q-database-with-python-081-strings-reverse-slice-palindrome","sec":"database-with-python-s082","q":"How do you check for a palindrome?","a":"<p>Compare the string with its reverse.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def is_palindrome(s): return s.lower() == s[::-1]\nprint(is_palindrome(&quot;radar&quot;))  # True</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0046","card":"q-database-with-python-082-strings-join-format-case-and-search","sec":"database-with-python-s083","q":"<code>str.join()</code> vs <code>str.format()</code>?","a":"<p><code>join()</code> concatenates an iterable with a separator. <code>format()</code> inserts values into placeholders.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>print(&quot; &quot;.join([&quot;a&quot;, &quot;b&quot;]))  # &quot;a b&quot;\nprint(&quot;{}-{}&quot;.format(1, 2))  # &quot;1-2&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0047","card":"q-database-with-python-082-strings-join-format-case-and-search","sec":"database-with-python-s083","q":"How do you change case?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>s = &quot;Hello&quot;; print(s.lower())  # &quot;hello&quot;; print(s.upper())  # &quot;HELLO&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0048","card":"q-database-with-python-082-strings-join-format-case-and-search","sec":"database-with-python-s083","q":"<code>find()</code> vs <code>index()</code>?","a":"<p><code>find()</code> returns the index or <code>-1</code> if not found. <code>index()</code> returns the index or raises <code>ValueError</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>s = &quot;hello&quot;; print(s.find(&quot;x&quot;))  # -1; print(s.index(&quot;l&quot;))  # 2</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0049","card":"q-database-with-python-082-strings-join-format-case-and-search","sec":"database-with-python-s083","q":"How do you remove leading and trailing whitespace?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>s = &quot;  hi  &quot;; print(s.strip())  # &quot;hi&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0050","card":"q-database-with-python-082-strings-join-format-case-and-search","sec":"database-with-python-s083","q":"How do you count substring occurrences?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>s = &quot;hello hello&quot;; print(s.count(&quot;hello&quot;))  # 2</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0051","card":"q-database-with-python-082-strings-join-format-case-and-search","sec":"database-with-python-s083","q":"What are f-strings?","a":"<p>Concise formatting with <code>f\"...\"</code>. They are faster and cleaner than <code>%</code> or <code>.format()</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name = &quot;Alice&quot;; print(f&quot;Hi, {name}&quot;)  # &quot;Hi, Alice&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0052","card":"q-database-with-python-082-strings-join-format-case-and-search","sec":"database-with-python-s083","q":"How do you split a string into a list?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>s = &quot;hello world&quot;; print(s.split())  # [&quot;hello&quot;, &quot;world&quot;]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0053","card":"q-database-with-python-083-lists-duplicates-comprehensions-sorting","sec":"database-with-python-s084","q":"How do you remove duplicates from a list?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>lst = [1, 2, 2]; print(list(set(lst)))  # [1, 2]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0054","card":"q-database-with-python-083-lists-duplicates-comprehensions-sorting","sec":"database-with-python-s084","q":"What is a list comprehension?","a":"<p>A concise way to build a list.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>squares = [x**2 for x in range(5)]; print(squares)  # [0, 1, 4, 9, 16]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0055","card":"q-database-with-python-083-lists-duplicates-comprehensions-sorting","sec":"database-with-python-s084","q":"How do you sort a list of dicts by a key?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>lst = [{&quot;age&quot;: 25}, {&quot;age&quot;: 20}]; print(sorted(lst, key=lambda x: x[&quot;age&quot;]))  # [{&quot;age&quot;: 20}, {&quot;age&quot;: 25}]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0056","card":"q-database-with-python-083-lists-duplicates-comprehensions-sorting","sec":"database-with-python-s084","q":"<code>append()</code> vs <code>extend()</code>?","a":"<p><code>append()</code> adds one item. <code>extend()</code> adds each element of an iterable.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>lst = [1]; lst.append([2, 3]); print(lst)  # [1, [2, 3]]\nlst = [1]; lst.extend([2, 3]); print(lst)  # [1, 2, 3]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0057","card":"q-database-with-python-083-lists-duplicates-comprehensions-sorting","sec":"database-with-python-s084","q":"<code>pop()</code> vs <code>remove()</code>?","a":"<p><code>pop()</code> removes by index and returns the value. <code>remove()</code> removes by value.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>lst = [1, 2]; print(lst.pop(0))  # 1; lst.remove(2); print(lst)  # []</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0058","card":"q-database-with-python-083-lists-duplicates-comprehensions-sorting","sec":"database-with-python-s084","q":"How do you flatten a nested list?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>nested = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]; flat = [x for sub in nested for x in sub]; print(flat)  # [1, 2, 3, 4]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0059","card":"q-database-with-python-084-dictionaries-and-sets","sec":"database-with-python-s085","q":"How do you merge two dictionaries?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>d1 = {&quot;a&quot;: 1}; d2 = {&quot;b&quot;: 2}; print(d1 | d2)  # {&quot;a&quot;: 1, &quot;b&quot;: 2} (Python 3.9+)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0060","card":"q-database-with-python-084-dictionaries-and-sets","sec":"database-with-python-s085","q":"How do you check if a key exists?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>d = {&quot;a&quot;: 1}; print(&quot;a&quot; in d)  # True; print(d.get(&quot;b&quot;, 0))  # 0</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0061","card":"q-database-with-python-084-dictionaries-and-sets","sec":"database-with-python-s085","q":"What is a dict comprehension?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>d = {x: x**2 for x in range(3)}; print(d)  # {0: 0, 1: 1, 2: 4}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0062","card":"q-database-with-python-084-dictionaries-and-sets","sec":"database-with-python-s085","q":"How do set operations work?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>s1 = {1, 2}; s2 = {2, 3}\nprint(s1 | s2)  # {1, 2, 3} (union)\nprint(s1 &amp; s2)  # {2} (intersection)\nprint(s1 - s2)  # {1} (difference)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0063","card":"q-database-with-python-085-functions-lambda-map-filter-reduce","sec":"database-with-python-s086","q":"What is a lambda and when do you use it?","a":"<p>An anonymous function for short tasks such as sorting keys.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>f = lambda x: x+1; print(f(2))  # 3</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0064","card":"q-database-with-python-085-functions-lambda-map-filter-reduce","sec":"database-with-python-s086","q":"<code>map()</code> vs <code>filter()</code> vs <code>reduce()</code>?","a":"<p><code>map()</code> transforms items, <code>filter()</code> selects items, <code>reduce()</code> aggregates items.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>print(list(map(lambda x: x*2, [1, 2])))  # [2, 4]\nprint(list(filter(lambda x: x &gt; 1, [1, 2])))  # [2]\nfrom functools import reduce; print(reduce(lambda x, y: x+y, [1, 2]))  # 3</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0065","card":"q-database-with-python-085-functions-lambda-map-filter-reduce","sec":"database-with-python-s086","q":"How do you define default arguments?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def func(x=1): print(x); func()  # 1</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0066","card":"q-database-with-python-085-functions-lambda-map-filter-reduce","sec":"database-with-python-s086","q":"How do you pass a function as an argument?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def call(f): f(); call(lambda: print(&quot;Hi&quot;))  # &quot;Hi&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0067","card":"q-database-with-python-086-functions-recursion-scope-decorators","sec":"database-with-python-s087","q":"What is recursion?","a":"<p>A function that calls itself, with a base case.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def fact(n): return 1 if n == 0 else n * fact(n-1)\nprint(fact(5))  # 120</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0068","card":"q-database-with-python-086-functions-recursion-scope-decorators","sec":"database-with-python-s087","q":"How does Python resolve variable scope (LEGB)?","a":"<p>Local, Enclosing, Global, Built-in.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>x = &quot;global&quot;; def f(): x = &quot;local&quot;; print(x); f()  # &quot;local&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0069","card":"q-database-with-python-086-functions-recursion-scope-decorators","sec":"database-with-python-s087","q":"What are decorators and how do you create one?","a":"<p>They modify a function using <code>@decorator</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def deco(func):\n    def wrapper(): print(&quot;Before&quot;); func()\n    return wrapper\n@deco\ndef hi(): print(&quot;Hi&quot;)\nhi()  # &quot;Before&quot;, &quot;Hi&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0070","card":"q-database-with-python-086-functions-recursion-scope-decorators","sec":"database-with-python-s087","q":"Why does the <code>global</code> keyword exist?","a":"<p>It lets a function modify a global variable.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>x = 1\ndef f():\n    global x\n    x = 2\n\nf()\nprint(x)  # 2</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0071","card":"q-database-with-python-087-copying-objects-and-exception-handling-i","sec":"database-with-python-s088","q":"Shallow vs deep copy?","a":"<p>A shallow copy copies the top level and references nested objects. A deep copy copies every level.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import copy\nlst = [[1]]\ns = copy.copy(lst)\nd = copy.deepcopy(lst)\ns[0][0] = 2\nprint(lst)  # [[2]]\nprint(d)  # [[1]]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0072","card":"q-database-with-python-087-copying-objects-and-exception-handling-i","sec":"database-with-python-s088","q":"How do you handle exceptions in a function?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def div(a, b):\n    try:\n        return a / b\n    except ZeroDivisionError:\n        return &quot;Error&quot;\n\nprint(div(1, 0))  # &quot;Error&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0073","card":"q-database-with-python-088-oop-basics-classes-inheritance-overridin","sec":"database-with-python-s089","q":"What are the key OOP principles?","a":"<p>Encapsulation, inheritance, polymorphism, abstraction. A class is a blueprint and an object is an instance.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class C:\n    pass\n\nobj = C()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0074","card":"q-database-with-python-088-oop-basics-classes-inheritance-overridin","sec":"database-with-python-s089","q":"How does inheritance work?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class A:\n    def x(self):\n        print(&quot;A&quot;)\n\nclass B(A):\n    pass\n\nB().x()  # &quot;A&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0075","card":"q-database-with-python-088-oop-basics-classes-inheritance-overridin","sec":"database-with-python-s089","q":"What is method overriding?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class A:\n    def x(self):\n        print(&quot;A&quot;)\n\nclass B(A):\n    def x(self):\n        print(&quot;B&quot;)\n\nB().x()  # &quot;B&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0076","card":"q-database-with-python-088-oop-basics-classes-inheritance-overridin","sec":"database-with-python-s089","q":"What is the purpose of <code>__init__</code>?","a":"<p>It initializes an instance.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class C:\n    def __init__(self, x):\n        self.x = x\n\nc = C(5)\nprint(c.x)  # 5</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0077","card":"q-database-with-python-089-oop-self-vs-cls-static-vs-class-methods","sec":"database-with-python-s090","q":"<code>self</code> vs <code>cls</code>?","a":"<p><code>self</code> refers to the instance. <code>cls</code> refers to the class.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class C:\n    @classmethod\n    def f(cls):\n        print(cls)\n\nC.f()  # &quot;&lt;class &#x27;__main__.C&#x27;&gt;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0078","card":"q-database-with-python-089-oop-self-vs-cls-static-vs-class-methods","sec":"database-with-python-s090","q":"Static vs class methods?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class C:\n    @staticmethod\n    def s():\n        print(&quot;Static&quot;)\n\n    @classmethod\n    def c(cls):\n        print(&quot;Class&quot;)\n\nC.s()\nC.c()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0079","card":"q-database-with-python-090-oop-polymorphism-encapsulation-abstract","sec":"database-with-python-s091","q":"Show polymorphism.","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class Dog:\n    def sound(self):\n        return &quot;Woof&quot;\n\nclass Cat:\n    def sound(self):\n        return &quot;Meow&quot;\n\nfor a in [Dog(), Cat()]:\n    print(a.sound())  # &quot;Woof&quot;, &quot;Meow&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0080","card":"q-database-with-python-090-oop-polymorphism-encapsulation-abstract","sec":"database-with-python-s091","q":"Show encapsulation.","a":"<p>A double underscore makes an attribute private (name-mangled), exposed through a method.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class C:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.__x = 1\n\n    def get(self):\n        return self.__x\n\nc = C()\nprint(c.get())  # 1</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0081","card":"q-database-with-python-090-oop-polymorphism-encapsulation-abstract","sec":"database-with-python-s091","q":"What are abstract base classes (ABCs)?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from abc import ABC, abstractmethod\n\nclass A(ABC):\n    @abstractmethod\n    def m(self):\n        pass\n\nclass B(A):\n    def m(self):\n        print(&quot;B&quot;)\n\nB().m()  # &quot;B&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0082","card":"q-database-with-python-090-oop-polymorphism-encapsulation-abstract","sec":"database-with-python-s091","q":"<code>__str__</code> vs <code>__repr__</code>?","a":"<p><code>__str__</code> is the user-friendly representation. <code>__repr__</code> is the developer and debugging representation.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class C:\n    def __str__(self): return &quot;Hi&quot;\n    def __repr__(self): return &quot;C()&quot;\n\nc = C()\nprint(str(c))  # &quot;Hi&quot;\nprint(repr(c))  # &quot;C()&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0083","card":"q-database-with-python-091-data-structures-stack-and-queue","sec":"database-with-python-s092","q":"How do you implement a stack?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class Stack:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.s = []\n\n    def push(self, x):\n        self.s.append(x)\n\n    def pop(self):\n        return self.s.pop() if self.s else None\n\ns = Stack()\ns.push(1)\nprint(s.pop())  # 1</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0084","card":"q-database-with-python-091-data-structures-stack-and-queue","sec":"database-with-python-s092","q":"How do you implement a queue?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from collections import deque\n\nclass Queue:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.q = deque()\n\n    def enqueue(self, x):\n        self.q.append(x)\n\n    def dequeue(self):\n        return self.q.popleft() if self.q else None\n\nq = Queue()\nq.enqueue(1)\nprint(q.dequeue())  # 1</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0085","card":"q-database-with-python-092-algorithms-binary-search-linked-lists-ma","sec":"database-with-python-s093","q":"How do you do binary search?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def binary_search(arr, x):\n    l, r = 0, len(arr) - 1\n    while l &lt;= r:\n        m = (l + r) // 2\n        if arr[m] == x:\n            return m\n        elif arr[m] &lt; x:\n            l = m + 1\n        else:\n            r = m - 1\n    return -1\n\nprint(binary_search([1, 3, 5], 3))  # 1</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0086","card":"q-database-with-python-092-algorithms-binary-search-linked-lists-ma","sec":"database-with-python-s093","q":"How do you reverse a linked list?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class Node:\n    def __init__(self, data):\n        self.data = data\n        self.next = None\n\ndef reverse(head):\n    prev, curr = None, head\n    while curr:\n        next_n = curr.next\n        curr.next = prev\n        prev = curr\n        curr = next_n\n    return prev\n\nhead = Node(1)\nhead.next = Node(2)\nhead = reverse(head)\nprint(head.data)  # 2</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0087","card":"q-database-with-python-092-algorithms-binary-search-linked-lists-ma","sec":"database-with-python-s093","q":"How do you detect a cycle in a linked list?","a":"<p>Floyd's method: step a slow and a fast iterator, and a cycle exists if they meet.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def has_cycle(head):\n    slow = fast = head\n    while fast and fast.next:\n        slow = slow.next\n        fast = fast.next.next\n        if slow == fast:\n            return True\n    return False</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0088","card":"q-database-with-python-092-algorithms-binary-search-linked-lists-ma","sec":"database-with-python-s093","q":"How do you find the max without <code>max()</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def find_max(lst):\n    m = lst[0]\n    for x in lst:\n        m = x if x &gt; m else m\n    return m\n\nprint(find_max([1, 5, 3]))  # 5</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0089","card":"q-database-with-python-093-data-structures-hash-table-heap-complexi","sec":"database-with-python-s094","q":"How do you implement a hash table?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class HashTable:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.t = [[] for _ in range(10)]\n\n    def put(self, k, v):\n        i = hash(k) % 10\n        self.t[i].append((k, v))\n\n    def get(self, k):\n        i = hash(k) % 10\n        return next((v for x, v in self.t[i] if x == k), None)\n\nht = HashTable()\nht.put(&quot;a&quot;, 1)\nprint(ht.get(&quot;a&quot;))  # 1</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0090","card":"q-database-with-python-093-data-structures-hash-table-heap-complexi","sec":"database-with-python-s094","q":"How do you use a heap?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import heapq\n\nh = [3, 1, 4]\nheapq.heapify(h)\nprint(heapq.heappop(h))  # 1</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0091","card":"q-database-with-python-093-data-structures-hash-table-heap-complexi","sec":"database-with-python-s094","q":"What is the time complexity of list operations?","a":"<p><code>append</code> O(1), <code>pop()</code> O(1), <code>pop(i)</code> and <code>insert</code> O(n), <code>remove</code> O(n), <code>in</code> O(n).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0092","card":"q-database-with-python-093-data-structures-hash-table-heap-complexi","sec":"database-with-python-s094","q":"BFS vs DFS?","a":"<p>BFS uses a queue and goes level by level, O(V+E). DFS uses a stack or recursion and goes depth first, O(V+E).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0093","card":"q-database-with-python-094-file-handling-read-and-write","sec":"database-with-python-s095","q":"How do you read a file line by line?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>with open(&quot;file.txt&quot;) as f:\n    [print(line.strip()) for line in f]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0094","card":"q-database-with-python-094-file-handling-read-and-write","sec":"database-with-python-s095","q":"<code>read()</code> vs <code>readline()</code> vs <code>readlines()</code>?","a":"<p><code>read()</code> returns all content, <code>readline()</code> one line, <code>readlines()</code> all lines as a list.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>with open(&quot;file.txt&quot;) as f:\n    print(f.read())</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0095","card":"q-database-with-python-094-file-handling-read-and-write","sec":"database-with-python-s095","q":"How do you write and append to a file?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>with open(&quot;file.txt&quot;, &quot;w&quot;) as f:\n    f.write(&quot;Hi&quot;)\n\nwith open(&quot;file.txt&quot;, &quot;a&quot;) as f:\n    f.write(&quot;More&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0096","card":"q-database-with-python-094-file-handling-read-and-write","sec":"database-with-python-s095","q":"How do you handle file exceptions?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>try:\n    open(&quot;file.txt&quot;)\nexcept FileNotFoundError:\n    print(&quot;Not found&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0097","card":"q-database-with-python-095-file-handling-csv-json-binary-delete","sec":"database-with-python-s096","q":"How do you read and write CSV?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import csv\n\nwith open(&quot;data.csv&quot;, &quot;w&quot;, newline=&quot;&quot;) as f:\n    csv.writer(f).writerow([&quot;a&quot;, 1])</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0098","card":"q-database-with-python-095-file-handling-csv-json-binary-delete","sec":"database-with-python-s096","q":"How do you work with JSON files?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import json\n\nwith open(&quot;data.json&quot;, &quot;w&quot;) as f:\n    json.dump({&quot;a&quot;: 1}, f)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0099","card":"q-database-with-python-095-file-handling-csv-json-binary-delete","sec":"database-with-python-s096","q":"Binary vs text modes?","a":"<p>Text modes <code>\"r\"</code> and <code>\"w\"</code> use strings. Binary modes <code>\"rb\"</code> and <code>\"wb\"</code> use bytes.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>with open(&quot;file.bin&quot;, &quot;wb&quot;) as f:\n    f.write(b&quot;Hi&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0100","card":"q-database-with-python-095-file-handling-csv-json-binary-delete","sec":"database-with-python-s096","q":"How do you delete a file?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import os\nos.remove(&quot;file.txt&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0101","card":"q-database-with-python-096-modules-and-libraries","sec":"database-with-python-s097","q":"<code>import</code> vs <code>from module import *</code>?","a":"<p><code>import</code> keeps names in a namespace. <code>from ... import *</code> gives direct access but risks name conflicts.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import math\nprint(math.pi)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0102","card":"q-database-with-python-096-modules-and-libraries","sec":"database-with-python-s097","q":"How do you install a library?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>pip install requests</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0103","card":"q-database-with-python-096-modules-and-libraries","sec":"database-with-python-s097","q":"What is the <code>sys</code> module for?","a":"<p>System-level access such as <code>sys.argv</code> and <code>sys.exit()</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import sys\nprint(sys.argv)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0104","card":"q-database-with-python-096-modules-and-libraries","sec":"database-with-python-s097","q":"How do you generate random numbers, use dates and the OS?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import random\nprint(random.randint(1, 10))  # 1-10\n\nfrom datetime import datetime\nprint(datetime.now())\n\nimport os\nprint(os.getcwd())</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0105","card":"q-database-with-python-097-modules-numpy-venv-collections-regex","sec":"database-with-python-s098","q":"NumPy vs lists?","a":"<p>NumPy arrays are fast and fixed-type. Lists are flexible but slower.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import numpy as np\nprint(np.array([1, 2]) + 1)  # [2, 3]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0106","card":"q-database-with-python-097-modules-numpy-venv-collections-regex","sec":"database-with-python-s098","q":"How do you create a virtual environment?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>python -m venv env\nsource env/bin/activate</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0107","card":"q-database-with-python-097-modules-numpy-venv-collections-regex","sec":"database-with-python-s098","q":"What is <code>collections</code> for?","a":"<p>Specialized containers such as <code>Counter</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from collections import Counter\nprint(Counter(&quot;aba&quot;))  # {&#x27;a&#x27;: 2, &#x27;b&#x27;: 1}</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0108","card":"q-database-with-python-097-modules-numpy-venv-collections-regex","sec":"database-with-python-s098","q":"How do you use regex?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import re\nprint(re.findall(r&quot;\\d+&quot;, &quot;12ab34&quot;))  # [&#x27;12&#x27;, &#x27;34&#x27;]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0109","card":"q-database-with-python-098-exception-handling","sec":"database-with-python-s099","q":"What is exception handling?","a":"<p>It manages runtime errors so the program does not crash, which makes it robust.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0110","card":"q-database-with-python-098-exception-handling","sec":"database-with-python-s099","q":"How do <code>try</code>, <code>except</code>, <code>else</code> and <code>finally</code> work?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>try:\n    x = 1 / 0\nexcept ZeroDivisionError:\n    print(&quot;Error&quot;)\nelse:\n    print(&quot;OK&quot;)\nfinally:\n    print(&quot;Done&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0111","card":"q-database-with-python-098-exception-handling","sec":"database-with-python-s099","q":"How do you raise a custom exception?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class MyError(Exception):\n    pass\n\nraise MyError(&quot;Oops&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0112","card":"q-database-with-python-098-exception-handling","sec":"database-with-python-s099","q":"Error vs exception?","a":"<p>An error is any issue (such as a syntax error). An exception is a catchable runtime error.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0113","card":"q-database-with-python-098-exception-handling","sec":"database-with-python-s099","q":"How do you catch several exceptions?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>try:\n    int(&quot;a&quot;)\nexcept (ValueError, TypeError):\n    print(&quot;Error&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0114","card":"q-database-with-python-099-exceptions-logging-assert-keyerror-exit","sec":"database-with-python-s100","q":"How do you log exceptions?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import logging\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.ERROR)\n\ntry:\n    1 / 0\nexcept:\n    logging.error(&quot;Fail&quot;, exc_info=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0115","card":"q-database-with-python-099-exceptions-logging-assert-keyerror-exit","sec":"database-with-python-s100","q":"What does <code>assert</code> do?","a":"<p>It raises <code>AssertionError</code> if the condition fails.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>assert 1 == 2, &quot;Wrong&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0116","card":"q-database-with-python-099-exceptions-logging-assert-keyerror-exit","sec":"database-with-python-s100","q":"How do you handle <code>KeyError</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>d = {&quot;a&quot;: 1}\nprint(d.get(&quot;b&quot;, 0))  # 0</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0117","card":"q-database-with-python-099-exceptions-logging-assert-keyerror-exit","sec":"database-with-python-s100","q":"<code>sys.exit()</code> vs raising an exception?","a":"<p><code>sys.exit()</code> stops the program. An exception is a catchable error.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import sys\nsys.exit(1)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0118","card":"q-database-with-python-100-advanced-python-generators-context-manag","sec":"database-with-python-s101","q":"What are generators?","a":"<p>Lazy iterators that use <code>yield</code>, unlike functions that return everything at once.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def gen():\n    yield 1\n    yield 2\n\nprint(next(gen()))  # 1</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0119","card":"q-database-with-python-100-advanced-python-generators-context-manag","sec":"database-with-python-s101","q":"How do you create a generator with <code>yield</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def gen(n):\n    for i in range(n):\n        yield i\n\nprint(list(gen(3)))  # [0, 1, 2]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0120","card":"q-database-with-python-100-advanced-python-generators-context-manag","sec":"database-with-python-s101","q":"What is a context manager?","a":"<p>An object that manages a resource with <code>__enter__</code> and <code>__exit__</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class CM:\n    def __enter__(self):\n        return self\n\n    def __exit__(self, *args):\n        pass\n\nwith CM():\n    print(&quot;Hi&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0121","card":"q-database-with-python-100-advanced-python-generators-context-manag","sec":"database-with-python-s101","q":"What are metaclasses?","a":"<p>Classes that create classes, used to customize class creation.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class Meta(type):\n    pass\n\nclass C(metaclass=Meta):\n    pass</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0122","card":"q-database-with-python-101-advanced-python-threads-processes-asynci","sec":"database-with-python-s102","q":"What are multithreading and the GIL?","a":"<p>The GIL limits CPU-bound parallelism in CPython, so threads are good for I/O.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import threading\nt = threading.Thread(target=lambda: print(&quot;Hi&quot;))\nt.start()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0123","card":"q-database-with-python-101-advanced-python-threads-processes-asynci","sec":"database-with-python-s102","q":"Multiprocessing vs multithreading?","a":"<p>Multithreading shares memory and is GIL-limited. Multiprocessing uses separate memory and has no GIL.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from multiprocessing import Process\nProcess(target=lambda: print(&quot;Hi&quot;)).start()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0124","card":"q-database-with-python-101-advanced-python-threads-processes-asynci","sec":"database-with-python-s102","q":"What is <code>asyncio</code>?","a":"<p>Python's async programming library.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import asyncio\n\nasync def f():\n    await asyncio.sleep(1)\n    print(&quot;Hi&quot;)\n\nasyncio.run(f())</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0125","card":"q-database-with-python-101-advanced-python-threads-processes-asynci","sec":"database-with-python-s102","q":"What are closures?","a":"<p>Nested functions that keep the outer scope.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def outer(x):\n    def inner():\n        return x\n    return inner\n\nf = outer(5)\nprint(f())  # 5</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0126","card":"q-database-with-python-101-advanced-python-threads-processes-asynci","sec":"database-with-python-s102","q":"How do you profile a Python program?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import cProfile\ncProfile.run(&quot;sum(range(1000))&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0127","card":"q-database-with-python-102-coding-problems-factorial-prime-fibonacc","sec":"database-with-python-s103","q":"Factorial of a number?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def fact(n):\n    return 1 if n &lt;= 0 else n * fact(n-1)\n\nprint(fact(5))  # 120</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0128","card":"q-database-with-python-102-coding-problems-factorial-prime-fibonacc","sec":"database-with-python-s103","q":"Check if a number is prime?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def is_prime(n):\n    if n &lt;= 1: return False\n    for i in range(2, int(n**0.5)+1):\n        if n % i == 0: return False\n    return True\n\nprint(is_prime(7))  # True</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0129","card":"q-database-with-python-102-coding-problems-factorial-prime-fibonacc","sec":"database-with-python-s103","q":"Fibonacci up to <code>n</code> terms?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def fib(n):\n    f = [0, 1]\n    for i in range(2, n):\n        f.append(f[-1] + f[-2])\n    return f[:n]\n\nprint(fib(5))  # [0, 1, 1, 2, 3]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0130","card":"q-database-with-python-102-coding-problems-factorial-prime-fibonacc","sec":"database-with-python-s103","q":"Remove vowels from a string?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def no_vowels(s):\n    return &quot;&quot;.join(c for c in s if c.lower() not in &quot;aeiou&quot;)\n\nprint(no_vowels(&quot;hello&quot;))  # &quot;hll&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0131","card":"q-database-with-python-103-coding-problems-second-largest-merge-rot","sec":"database-with-python-s104","q":"Second largest in a list?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def second_max(lst):\n    if len(lst) &lt; 2: return None\n    m1, m2 = max(lst[0], lst[1]), min(lst[0], lst[1])\n    for x in lst[2:]:\n        m1, m2 = (x, m1) if x &gt; m1 else (m1, x if x &gt; m2 else m2)\n    return m2\n\nprint(second_max([1, 5, 3]))  # 3</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0132","card":"q-database-with-python-103-coding-problems-second-largest-merge-rot","sec":"database-with-python-s104","q":"Merge two sorted lists?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def merge(l1, l2):\n    r, i, j = [], 0, 0\n    while i &lt; len(l1) and j &lt; len(l2):\n        if l1[i] &lt; l2[j]:\n            r.append(l1[i])\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            r.append(l2[j])\n            j += 1\n    return r + l1[i:] + l2[j:]\n\nprint(merge([1, 3], [2, 4]))  # [1, 2, 3, 4]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0133","card":"q-database-with-python-103-coding-problems-second-largest-merge-rot","sec":"database-with-python-s104","q":"Rotate a list by <code>k</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def rotate(lst, k):\n    k %= len(lst)\n    return lst[-k:] + lst[:-k]\n\nprint(rotate([1, 2, 3], 1))  # [3, 1, 2]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0134","card":"q-database-with-python-104-coding-problems-bst-anagrams-longest-com","sec":"database-with-python-s105","q":"Binary search tree insert?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class Node:\n    def __init__(self, v):\n        self.v = v\n        self.left = self.right = None\n\nclass BST:\n    def insert(self, root, v):\n        if not root: return Node(v)\n        if v &lt; root.v:\n            root.left = self.insert(root.left, v)\n        else:\n            root.right = self.insert(root.right, v)\n        return root\n\nbst = BST()\nroot = bst.insert(None, 5)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0135","card":"q-database-with-python-104-coding-problems-bst-anagrams-longest-com","sec":"database-with-python-s105","q":"Find anagrams in a list?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def anagrams(lst):\n    d = {}\n    for s in lst:\n        k = &quot;&quot;.join(sorted(s))\n        d.setdefault(k, []).append(s)\n    return [v for v in d.values() if len(v) &gt; 1]\n\nprint(anagrams([&quot;eat&quot;, &quot;tea&quot;, &quot;tan&quot;]))  # [[&#x27;eat&#x27;, &#x27;tea&#x27;]]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0136","card":"q-database-with-python-104-coding-problems-bst-anagrams-longest-com","sec":"database-with-python-s105","q":"Longest common substring?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def lcs(s1, s2):\n    dp = [[0]*(len(s2)+1) for _ in range(len(s1)+1)]\n    m, end = 0, 0\n    for i in range(1, len(s1)+1):\n        for j in range(1, len(s2)+1):\n            if s1[i-1] == s2[j-1]:\n                dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1] + 1\n                if dp[i][j] &gt; m:\n                    m = dp[i][j]\n                    end = i\n    return s1[end-m:end]\n\nprint(lcs(&quot;ABCD&quot;, &quot;ABED&quot;))  # &quot;AB&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0137","card":"q-database-with-python-105-practical-scenarios-performance-debuggin","sec":"database-with-python-s106","q":"How do you optimize a script for large datasets?","a":"<p>Use generators, NumPy or chunking.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def gen_data(n):\n    yield from range(n)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0138","card":"q-database-with-python-105-practical-scenarios-performance-debuggin","sec":"database-with-python-s106","q":"How do you debug a Python program?","a":"<p>Use <code>print()</code>, <code>pdb</code> or IDE breakpoints.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import pdb\npdb.set_trace()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0139","card":"q-database-with-python-105-practical-scenarios-performance-debuggin","sec":"database-with-python-s106","q":"How do you handle memory leaks?","a":"<p>Use <code>tracemalloc</code> and close resources.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import tracemalloc\ntracemalloc.start()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0140","card":"q-database-with-python-105-practical-scenarios-performance-debuggin","sec":"database-with-python-s106","q":"How do you process a large CSV without loading it all?","a":"<p>Stream it row by row.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import csv\nwith open(&quot;large.csv&quot;) as f:\n    [print(row) for row in csv.reader(f)]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0141","card":"q-database-with-python-106-practical-scenarios-rest-api-tests-cachi","sec":"database-with-python-s107","q":"How do you design a REST API with Flask?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from flask import Flask, jsonify\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route(&quot;/hi&quot;, methods=[&quot;GET&quot;])\ndef hi():\n    return jsonify({&quot;msg&quot;: &quot;Hello&quot;})\n\napp.run()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0142","card":"q-database-with-python-106-practical-scenarios-rest-api-tests-cachi","sec":"database-with-python-s107","q":"How do you unit test with <code>unittest</code> or <code>pytest</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def add(a, b):\n    return a + b\n\n# pytest\ndef test_add():\n    assert add(2, 3) == 5</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0143","card":"q-database-with-python-106-practical-scenarios-rest-api-tests-cachi","sec":"database-with-python-s107","q":"How do you add simple caching?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from functools import lru_cache\n\n@lru_cache\ndef f(x):\n    return x * x\n\nprint(f(5))  # Cached</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0144","card":"q-database-with-python-106-practical-scenarios-rest-api-tests-cachi","sec":"database-with-python-s107","q":"How do you scrape a website?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import requests, bs4\nsoup = bs4.BeautifulSoup(requests.get(&quot;http://example.com&quot;).text, &quot;html.parser&quot;)\nprint(soup.h1.text)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0145","card":"q-database-with-python-107-practical-scenarios-concurrency-and-depl","sec":"database-with-python-s108","q":"How do you handle concurrency in a web app?","a":"<p>Use <code>asyncio</code> or <code>gunicorn</code> workers.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>gunicorn -w 4 app:app</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0146","card":"q-database-with-python-107-practical-scenarios-concurrency-and-depl","sec":"database-with-python-s108","q":"How do you deploy a Python app to production?","a":"<p>Use Docker, gunicorn and a virtualenv.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Dockerfile</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>FROM python:3.9\nCOPY . .\nRUN pip install -r requirements.txt\nCMD [&quot;gunicorn&quot;, &quot;app:app&quot;]</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0147","card":"q-database-with-python-108-connection-timeout-error","sec":"database-with-python-s109","q":"A <code>snowflake.connector</code> connection times out. How do you troubleshoot it?","a":"<p>Check network reachability, firewall rules for outbound 443, the Snowflake account configuration and the connection parameters. Set a login timeout and a network timeout, test the socket, then retry with a longer timeout.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport logging\nimport socket\n\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.DEBUG)\n\ntry:\n    conn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n        user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;,\n        password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;,\n        account=&#x27;your_account.region.cloud&#x27;,\n        login_timeout=10,\n        network_timeout=30\n    )\n    logging.info(&quot;Connection successful&quot;)\nexcept snowflake.connector.errors.OperationalError as e:\n    logging.error(f&quot;Connection timeout: {e}&quot;)\n    try:\n        socket.create_connection((&quot;snowflake.com&quot;, 443), timeout=5)\n        logging.info(&quot;Network is reachable&quot;)\n    except socket.timeout:\n        logging.error(&quot;Network issue: unable to reach Snowflake&quot;)\n    logging.info(&quot;Check firewall rules for outbound connections to Snowflake&quot;)\n    conn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n        user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;,\n        password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;,\n        account=&#x27;your_account.region.cloud&#x27;,\n        login_timeout=30   # increased timeout\n    )\nfinally:\n    if &#x27;conn&#x27; in locals():\n        conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0148","card":"q-database-with-python-109-invalid-account-name","sec":"database-with-python-s110","q":"A script fails with \"Invalid account name provided.\" What do you verify?","a":"<p>The account URL format (<code>&lt;account&gt;.&lt;region&gt;.&lt;cloud&gt;</code> or just <code>&lt;account&gt;</code>), the region and the cloud provider (AWS, Azure, GCP). Check the account URL in the Snowflake admin console.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport logging\n\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.DEBUG)\n\ndef verify_account_name(account):\n    parts = account.split(&#x27;.&#x27;)\n    if len(parts) == 1:\n        logging.info(&quot;No region/cloud specified, assuming default&quot;)\n    elif len(parts) == 3:\n        logging.info(f&quot;Account: {parts[0]}, Region: {parts[1]}, Cloud: {parts[2]}&quot;)\n    else:\n        logging.error(&quot;Invalid account format&quot;)\n        return False\n    return True\n\ntry:\n    account = &#x27;your_account.region.cloud&#x27;   # e.g. myaccount.us-east-1.aws\n    if verify_account_name(account):\n        conn = snowflake.connector.connect(user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;, password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;, account=account)\n        logging.info(&quot;Connection successful&quot;)\n    else:\n        logging.error(&quot;Fix account name format and retry&quot;)\nexcept snowflake.connector.errors.DatabaseError as e:\n    logging.error(f&quot;Connection failed: {e}&quot;)\n    logging.info(&quot;Verify account name format: &lt;account&gt;.&lt;region&gt;.&lt;cloud&gt;&quot;)\nfinally:\n    if &#x27;conn&#x27; in locals():\n        conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0149","card":"q-database-with-python-110-missing-database-driver","sec":"database-with-python-s111","q":"A MySQL connection fails with \"No suitable driver found.\" What is the cause?","a":"<p>The driver (<code>mysql-connector-python</code> or <code>pymysql</code>) is not installed or not imported. Install it and import it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import logging\n\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.DEBUG)\n\ntry:\n    import mysql.connector\nexcept ImportError:\n    logging.error(&quot;MySQL driver not found. Installing mysql-connector-python&quot;)\n    import subprocess\n    subprocess.check_call([&#x27;pip&#x27;, &#x27;install&#x27;, &#x27;mysql-connector-python&#x27;])\n    import mysql.connector\n\ntry:\n    conn = mysql.connector.connect(\n        host=&#x27;localhost&#x27;,\n        user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;,\n        password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;,\n        database=&#x27;your_database&#x27;\n    )\n    logging.info(&quot;MySQL connection successful&quot;)\nexcept mysql.connector.Error as e:\n    logging.error(f&quot;Connection failed: {e}&quot;)\nfinally:\n    if &#x27;conn&#x27; in locals():\n        conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0150","card":"q-database-with-python-111-works-locally-fails-in-production-connec","sec":"database-with-python-s112","q":"A Snowflake script works locally but fails in production. Which parameters differ between environments?","a":"<p>Account, warehouse, database, schema, role and the environment-specific credentials. Load them per environment from configuration and environment variables.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport os\nimport logging\n\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.DEBUG)\n\ndef load_env_config(env=&#x27;prod&#x27;):\n    configs = {\n        &#x27;dev&#x27;: {&#x27;account&#x27;: &#x27;dev_account.region.cloud&#x27;, &#x27;warehouse&#x27;: &#x27;dev_warehouse&#x27;,\n                &#x27;database&#x27;: &#x27;dev_db&#x27;, &#x27;schema&#x27;: &#x27;dev_schema&#x27;, &#x27;role&#x27;: &#x27;dev_role&#x27;},\n        &#x27;prod&#x27;: {&#x27;account&#x27;: &#x27;prod_account.region.cloud&#x27;, &#x27;warehouse&#x27;: &#x27;prod_warehouse&#x27;,\n                 &#x27;database&#x27;: &#x27;prod_db&#x27;, &#x27;schema&#x27;: &#x27;prod_schema&#x27;, &#x27;role&#x27;: &#x27;prod_role&#x27;}\n    }\n    return configs.get(env, configs[&#x27;prod&#x27;])\n\ntry:\n    env = os.getenv(&#x27;ENV&#x27;, &#x27;prod&#x27;)\n    config = load_env_config(env)\n    conn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n        user=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_USER&#x27;),\n        password=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_PASSWORD&#x27;),\n        account=config[&#x27;account&#x27;],\n        warehouse=config[&#x27;warehouse&#x27;],\n        database=config[&#x27;database&#x27;],\n        schema=config[&#x27;schema&#x27;],\n        role=config[&#x27;role&#x27;]\n    )\n    logging.info(f&quot;Connected to Snowflake in {env} environment&quot;)\nexcept snowflake.connector.errors.OperationalError as e:\n    logging.error(f&quot;Connection failed: {e}&quot;)\n    logging.info(f&quot;Current config: {config}&quot;)\nfinally:\n    if &#x27;conn&#x27; in locals():\n        conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0151","card":"q-database-with-python-112-ssl-certificate-error","sec":"database-with-python-s113","q":"SSL certificate verification fails when connecting to Snowflake. How do you diagnose and fix it?","a":"<p>Check SSL settings, CA certificates and network proxies. <code>insecure_mode=True</code> bypasses verification and is only for debugging, never production. Point the CA bundle environment variable at the right certificate.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport logging\nimport os\n\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.DEBUG)\n\ntry:\n    conn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n        user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;,\n        password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;,\n        account=&#x27;your_account.region.cloud&#x27;,\n        insecure_mode=False   # default SSL verification\n    )\nexcept snowflake.connector.errors.OperationalError as e:\n    logging.error(f&quot;SSL error: {e}&quot;)\n    logging.warning(&quot;Attempting connection with insecure_mode=True (debugging only)&quot;)\n    conn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n        user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;,\n        password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;,\n        account=&#x27;your_account.region.cloud&#x27;,\n        insecure_mode=True\n    )\n    logging.info(&quot;Check CA certificates or proxy settings&quot;)\n    # os.environ[&#x27;REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE&#x27;] = &#x27;/path/to/ca-cert.pem&#x27;\nfinally:\n    if &#x27;conn&#x27; in locals():\n        conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0152","card":"q-database-with-python-113-connection-pooling-for-frequent-connecti","sec":"database-with-python-s114","q":"Frequent connection opens cause delays. How do you pool connections?","a":"<p>Use SQLAlchemy's <code>QueuePool</code> (<code>pool_size</code> is the base number of connections, <code>max_overflow</code> allows extras, <code>pool_timeout</code> is the wait for a free connection). Snowflake has no traditional client-side pooling, so keep connections minimal and reuse them.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from sqlalchemy import create_engine\nfrom sqlalchemy.pool import QueuePool\nimport snowflake.connector\nimport logging\n\nmysql_url = &quot;mysql+mysqlconnector://your_user:your_password@localhost/your_database&quot;\n\ntry:\n    mysql_engine = create_engine(\n        mysql_url,\n        poolclass=QueuePool,\n        pool_size=5,\n        max_overflow=10,\n        pool_timeout=30\n    )\n    with mysql_engine.connect() as conn:\n        conn.execute(&quot;SELECT 1&quot;)\n        logging.info(&quot;MySQL pooled connection successful&quot;)\n\n    snowflake_conn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n        user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;,\n        password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;,\n        account=&#x27;your_account.region.cloud&#x27;,\n        warehouse=&#x27;your_warehouse&#x27;,\n        database=&#x27;your_database&#x27;,\n        schema=&#x27;your_schema&#x27;\n    )\nexcept Exception as e:\n    logging.error(f&quot;Connection error: {e}&quot;)\nfinally:\n    if &#x27;snowflake_conn&#x27; in locals():\n        snowflake_conn.close()\n    if &#x27;mysql_engine&#x27; in locals():\n        mysql_engine.dispose()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0153","card":"q-database-with-python-114-environment-variable-mismatch","sec":"database-with-python-s115","q":"Credentials in environment variables are wrong. How do you verify and fix it?","a":"<p>Check that every required variable exists with <code>os.getenv()</code>, confirm names, load a <code>.env</code> file with <code>python-dotenv</code>, and report which variable is missing.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport os\nimport logging\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\n\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.DEBUG)\nload_dotenv()\n\ndef verify_env_vars():\n    required_vars = [&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_USER&#x27;, &#x27;SNOWFLAKE_PASSWORD&#x27;, &#x27;SNOWFLAKE_ACCOUNT&#x27;]\n    for var in required_vars:\n        if not os.getenv(var):\n            logging.error(f&quot;Missing environment variable: {var}&quot;)\n            return False\n    return True\n\ntry:\n    if verify_env_vars():\n        conn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n            user=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_USER&#x27;),\n            password=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_PASSWORD&#x27;),\n            account=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_ACCOUNT&#x27;),\n            warehouse=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_WAREHOUSE&#x27;, &#x27;default_warehouse&#x27;),\n            database=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_DATABASE&#x27;, &#x27;default_db&#x27;),\n            schema=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_SCHEMA&#x27;, &#x27;default_schema&#x27;)\n        )\n        logging.info(&quot;Connection successful&quot;)\n    else:\n        logging.info(&quot;Check .env file or system environment variables&quot;)\nexcept snowflake.connector.errors.DatabaseError as e:\n    logging.error(f&quot;Connection failed: {e}&quot;)\nfinally:\n    if &#x27;conn&#x27; in locals():\n        conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0154","card":"q-database-with-python-115-authentication-failure","sec":"database-with-python-s116","q":"A script fails with \"Authentication failed\". What do you check?","a":"<p>Username and password, key pair authentication, MFA and token expiration. For MFA use <code>authenticator='externalbrowser'</code> with a configured browser.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nfrom snowflake.connector.errors import DatabaseError\nimport os\n\ntry:\n    conn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n        user=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_USER&#x27;),\n        password=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_PASSWORD&#x27;),\n        account=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_ACCOUNT&#x27;),\n        authenticator=&#x27;snowflake&#x27;,   # &#x27;externalbrowser&#x27; for MFA/SSO\n        warehouse=&#x27;COMPUTE_WH&#x27;,\n        database=&#x27;TEST_DB&#x27;,\n        schema=&#x27;PUBLIC&#x27;\n    )\n    print(&quot;Connection successful&quot;)\nexcept DatabaseError as e:\n    if &quot;Authentication failed&quot; in str(e):\n        print(&quot;Authentication failed. Verify username, password, or MFA settings.&quot;)\n    raise</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0155","card":"q-database-with-python-116-hardcoded-credentials","sec":"database-with-python-s117","q":"You find hardcoded Snowflake credentials in code review. How do you refactor?","a":"<p>Move them to environment variables, a secret manager such as AWS Secrets Manager, or the <code>keyring</code> library.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport os\nimport boto3\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\n\nload_dotenv()\n\ndef get_snowflake_credentials(secret_name, region_name):\n    client = boto3.client(&#x27;secretsmanager&#x27;, region_name=region_name)\n    response = client.get_secret_value(SecretId=secret_name)\n    return response[&#x27;SecretString&#x27;].split(&#x27;:&#x27;)\n\nsecret_name = &quot;snowflake/credentials&quot;\nregion_name = &quot;us-west-2&quot;\nuser, password = (get_snowflake_credentials(secret_name, region_name)\n                  if os.getenv(&#x27;USE_SECRETS&#x27;)\n                  else (os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_USER&#x27;), os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_PASSWORD&#x27;)))\n\nconn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n    user=user,\n    password=password,\n    account=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_ACCOUNT&#x27;),\n    warehouse=&#x27;COMPUTE_WH&#x27;,\n    database=&#x27;TEST_DB&#x27;,\n    schema=&#x27;PUBLIC&#x27;\n)\nconn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0156","card":"q-database-with-python-117-insufficient-privileges","sec":"database-with-python-s118","q":"The script connects but queries fail with \"Insufficient privileges\". How do you diagnose it?","a":"<p>Check which role is active (<code>CURRENT_ROLE()</code>), grant the needed permissions, or connect with (or <code>USE ROLE</code>) the correct role.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport os\n\nconn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n    user=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_USER&#x27;),\n    password=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_PASSWORD&#x27;),\n    account=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_ACCOUNT&#x27;),\n    warehouse=&#x27;COMPUTE_WH&#x27;,\n    database=&#x27;TEST_DB&#x27;,\n    schema=&#x27;PUBLIC&#x27;,\n    role=&#x27;REQUIRED_ROLE&#x27;\n)\n\ncursor = conn.cursor()\ntry:\n    cursor.execute(&quot;SELECT CURRENT_ROLE()&quot;)\n    print(f&quot;Current role: {cursor.fetchone()[0]}&quot;)\n    cursor.execute(&quot;SELECT * FROM TEST_TABLE LIMIT 1&quot;)\nexcept snowflake.connector.errors.ProgrammingError as e:\n    if &quot;Insufficient privileges&quot; in str(e):\n        print(&quot;Insufficient privileges. Verify role permissions or use a different role.&quot;)\n        cursor.execute(&quot;USE ROLE REQUIRED_ROLE&quot;)\n    raise\nfinally:\n    conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0157","card":"q-database-with-python-118-key-pair-authentication-failure","sec":"database-with-python-s119","q":"Key pair auth fails with \"Invalid private key\". What is wrong?","a":"<p>Check the key format (PEM, PKCS8 <code>.p8</code>), the passphrase, file permissions (<code>chmod 600</code>) and the connector configuration.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport os\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives import serialization\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.backends import default_backend\n\nwith open(&quot;snowflake_key.p8&quot;, &quot;rb&quot;) as key_file:\n    private_key = serialization.load_pem_private_key(\n        key_file.read(),\n        password=os.getenv(&#x27;KEY_PASSPHRASE&#x27;).encode() if os.getenv(&#x27;KEY_PASSPHRASE&#x27;) else None,\n        backend=default_backend()\n    )\n\nos.chmod(&quot;snowflake_key.p8&quot;, 0o600)   # secure permissions\n\nconn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n    user=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_USER&#x27;),\n    private_key=private_key,\n    account=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_ACCOUNT&#x27;),\n    warehouse=&#x27;COMPUTE_WH&#x27;,\n    database=&#x27;TEST_DB&#x27;,\n    schema=&#x27;PUBLIC&#x27;\n)\nconn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0158","card":"q-database-with-python-119-sql-injection","sec":"database-with-python-s120","q":"A script builds MySQL queries by string concatenation. How do you prevent SQL injection?","a":"<p>Use parameterized queries (bind variables in the Snowflake connector, bound parameters in SQLAlchemy).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport os\nfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine\n\nconn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n    user=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_USER&#x27;),\n    password=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_PASSWORD&#x27;),\n    account=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_ACCOUNT&#x27;),\n    warehouse=&#x27;COMPUTE_WH&#x27;,\n    database=&#x27;TEST_DB&#x27;,\n    schema=&#x27;PUBLIC&#x27;\n)\nuser_input = &quot;user_input&quot;\ntry:\n    cursor = conn.cursor()\n    query = &quot;SELECT * FROM TEST_TABLE WHERE column_name = %s&quot;\n    cursor.execute(query, (user_input,))\n    results = cursor.fetchall()\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f&quot;Query error: {e}&quot;)\nfinally:\n    conn.close()\n\n# MySQL with SQLAlchemy\nengine = create_engine(f&quot;mysql+pymysql://{os.getenv(&#x27;MYSQL_USER&#x27;)}:{os.getenv(&#x27;MYSQL_PASSWORD&#x27;)}@localhost/TEST_DB&quot;)\nwith engine.connect() as conn:\n    result = conn.execute(&quot;SELECT * FROM TEST_TABLE WHERE column_name = %s&quot;, (user_input,))</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0159","card":"q-database-with-python-120-expired-oauth-token","sec":"database-with-python-s121","q":"OAuth authentication fails with \"Token expired\". How do you refresh the token?","a":"<p>Use the OAuth refresh-token flow, then connect with <code>authenticator='oauth'</code> and the new access token. On a \"Token expired\" error, refresh and reconnect.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport os\nimport requests\n\ndef refresh_oauth_token(refresh_token, client_id, client_secret):\n    url = &quot;https://&lt;snowflake_account&gt;.snowflakecomputing.com/oauth/token&quot;\n    data = {\n        &quot;grant_type&quot;: &quot;refresh_token&quot;,\n        &quot;refresh_token&quot;: refresh_token,\n        &quot;client_id&quot;: client_id,\n        &quot;client_secret&quot;: client_secret\n    }\n    response = requests.post(url, data=data)\n    return response.json()[&#x27;access_token&#x27;]\n\ndef connect_with_token(access_token):\n    return snowflake.connector.connect(\n        user=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_USER&#x27;),\n        account=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_ACCOUNT&#x27;),\n        authenticator=&#x27;oauth&#x27;,\n        token=access_token,\n        warehouse=&#x27;COMPUTE_WH&#x27;,\n        database=&#x27;TEST_DB&#x27;,\n        schema=&#x27;PUBLIC&#x27;\n    )\n\ntry:\n    access_token = refresh_oauth_token(\n        refresh_token=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_REFRESH_TOKEN&#x27;),\n        client_id=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_CLIENT_ID&#x27;),\n        client_secret=os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_CLIENT_SECRET&#x27;)\n    )\n    conn = connect_with_token(access_token)\nexcept snowflake.connector.errors.DatabaseError as e:\n    if &quot;Token expired&quot; in str(e):\n        print(&quot;Token expired. Refreshing token...&quot;)\n        access_token = refresh_oauth_token(\n            os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_REFRESH_TOKEN&#x27;),\n            os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_CLIENT_ID&#x27;),\n            os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_CLIENT_SECRET&#x27;)\n        )\n        conn = connect_with_token(access_token)\nfinally:\n    conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0160","card":"q-database-with-python-121-slow-query-in-snowflake","sec":"database-with-python-s122","q":"A complex Snowflake query is slow. How do you improve it?","a":"<p>Optimize the query (simplify joins and conditions, filter early), size the warehouse for the workload and use result caching so repeated queries are not recomputed.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nfrom snowflake.connector import DictCursor\n\nconn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n    user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;,\n    password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;,\n    account=&#x27;your_account&#x27;,\n    warehouse=&#x27;OPTIMIZED_WAREHOUSE&#x27;,   # appropriately sized warehouse\n    database=&#x27;your_db&#x27;,\n    schema=&#x27;your_schema&#x27;\n)\n\nquery = &quot;&quot;&quot;\nSELECT c.customer_id, c.name, COUNT(o.order_id) as order_count\nFROM customers c\nJOIN orders o ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id\nWHERE o.order_date &gt;= &#x27;2023-01-01&#x27;\nGROUP BY c.customer_id, c.name\nHAVING order_count &gt; 10\n&quot;&quot;&quot;\n\ntry:\n    cursor = conn.cursor(DictCursor)\n    cursor.execute(&quot;ALTER SESSION SET USE_CACHED_RESULT = TRUE&quot;)   # result caching\n    cursor.execute(query)\n    for row in cursor.fetchall():\n        print(row)\nfinally:\n    cursor.close()\n    conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0161","card":"q-database-with-python-122-query-timeout","sec":"database-with-python-s123","q":"A long query times out on Snowflake and on a generic SQL database. What do you do?","a":"<p>Look at query complexity, raise the timeout (<code>QUERY_TIMEOUT</code> session parameter for Snowflake, <code>connect_timeout</code> for MySQL), add indexes on frequently queried columns in MySQL, and break big queries into pages with <code>LIMIT</code>/<code>OFFSET</code>. Standard Snowflake tables have no user-created indexes, so rely on warehouse size and clustering instead.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport mysql.connector\nfrom snowflake.connector.errors import ProgrammingError\n\nsnowflake_conn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n    user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;,\n    password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;,\n    account=&#x27;your_account&#x27;,\n    warehouse=&#x27;your_warehouse&#x27;,\n    database=&#x27;your_db&#x27;,\n    schema=&#x27;your_schema&#x27;,\n    session_parameters={&#x27;QUERY_TIMEOUT&#x27;: 300}   # 5 minutes\n)\n\nmysql_conn = mysql.connector.connect(\n    host=&#x27;localhost&#x27;,\n    user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;,\n    password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;,\n    database=&#x27;your_db&#x27;,\n    connect_timeout=300\n)\n\nsnowflake_query = &quot;&quot;&quot;\nSELECT * FROM large_table\nWHERE date_column BETWEEN &#x27;2023-01-01&#x27; AND &#x27;2023-12-31&#x27;\n&quot;&quot;&quot;\nmysql_query = &quot;&quot;&quot;\nSELECT * FROM large_table\nWHERE date_column BETWEEN &#x27;2023-01-01&#x27; AND &#x27;2023-12-31&#x27;\nLIMIT 1000 OFFSET %s\n&quot;&quot;&quot;\n\ntry:\n    snowflake_cursor = snowflake_conn.cursor()\n    snowflake_cursor.execute(snowflake_query)\n    snowflake_results = snowflake_cursor.fetchall()\n\n    mysql_cursor = mysql_conn.cursor()\n    offset = 0\n    while True:\n        mysql_cursor.execute(mysql_query, (offset,))\n        results = mysql_cursor.fetchall()\n        if not results:\n            break\n        offset += 1000\nexcept ProgrammingError as e:\n    print(f&quot;Snowflake Error: {e}&quot;)\nexcept mysql.connector.Error as e:\n    print(f&quot;MySQL Error: {e}&quot;)\nfinally:\n    snowflake_cursor.close()\n    snowflake_conn.close()\n    mysql_cursor.close()\n    mysql_conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0162","card":"q-database-with-python-123-large-result-set-and-memory","sec":"database-with-python-s124","q":"A large result set causes memory problems. How do you handle it?","a":"<p>Fetch in chunks with <code>fetchmany()</code> and process each chunk (for example, append to a CSV with pandas). The connector's <code>fetch_pandas_all()</code> is another option for smaller sets.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport pandas as pd\n\nconn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n    user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;, password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;, account=&#x27;your_account&#x27;,\n    warehouse=&#x27;your_warehouse&#x27;, database=&#x27;your_db&#x27;, schema=&#x27;your_schema&#x27;\n)\n\ntry:\n    cursor = conn.cursor()\n    cursor.execute(&quot;SELECT * FROM large_table&quot;)\n    chunk_size = 10000\n    while True:\n        rows = cursor.fetchmany(chunk_size)\n        if not rows:\n            break\n        df = pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=[desc[0] for desc in cursor.description])\n        df.to_csv(&#x27;output.csv&#x27;, mode=&#x27;a&#x27;, index=False)\nfinally:\n    cursor.close()\n    conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0163","card":"q-database-with-python-124-inconsistent-query-results","sec":"database-with-python-s125","q":"A Snowflake query returns different results across runs. What could cause it and how do you investigate?","a":"<p>Data updates between runs, result caching, transaction isolation and query logic errors. Disable the result cache to force fresh data, log the results, and check the query conditions. Snowflake's transaction isolation is READ COMMITTED.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nfrom snowflake.connector import DictCursor\n\nconn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n    user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;, password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;, account=&#x27;your_account&#x27;,\n    warehouse=&#x27;your_warehouse&#x27;, database=&#x27;your_db&#x27;, schema=&#x27;your_schema&#x27;\n)\n\nquery = &quot;&quot;&quot;\nSELECT * FROM orders\nWHERE order_date = CURRENT_DATE\n&quot;&quot;&quot;\n\ntry:\n    cursor = conn.cursor(DictCursor)\n    cursor.execute(&quot;ALTER SESSION SET USE_CACHED_RESULT = FALSE&quot;)   # fresh data\n    cursor.execute(query)\n    results = cursor.fetchall()\n\n    with open(&#x27;query_log.txt&#x27;, &#x27;a&#x27;) as f:\n        f.write(str(results))\n\n    if not results:\n        print(&quot;No results returned. Verify query conditions.&quot;)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f&quot;Error: {e}&quot;)\nfinally:\n    cursor.close()\n    conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0164","card":"q-database-with-python-125-batch-insert-performance","sec":"database-with-python-s126","q":"Inserting thousands of rows into Snowflake is slow. How do you optimize it?","a":"<p>Use bulk loading: <code>write_pandas</code> for DataFrames, or <code>PUT</code> a file to a stage and <code>COPY INTO</code> the table. Tune the batch size and run loads in parallel.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom snowflake.connector.pandas_tools import write_pandas\n\nconn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n    user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;, password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;, account=&#x27;your_account&#x27;,\n    warehouse=&#x27;your_warehouse&#x27;, database=&#x27;your_db&#x27;, schema=&#x27;your_schema&#x27;\n)\n\ndata = pd.DataFrame({\n    &#x27;id&#x27;: range(10000),\n    &#x27;name&#x27;: [f&#x27;name_{i}&#x27; for i in range(10000)],\n    &#x27;value&#x27;: [i * 1.5 for i in range(10000)]\n})\n\ntry:\n    success, nchunks, nrows, _ = write_pandas(\n        conn=conn, df=data, table_name=&#x27;target_table&#x27;, auto_create_table=True\n    )\n    print(f&quot;Inserted {nrows} rows in {nchunks} chunks&quot;)\n\n    # Alternative: COPY INTO from a stage\n    cursor = conn.cursor()\n    cursor.execute(&quot;PUT file://data.csv @my_stage&quot;)\n    cursor.execute(&quot;&quot;&quot;\n    COPY INTO target_table\n    FROM @my_stage/data.csv\n    FILE_FORMAT = (TYPE = CSV SKIP_HEADER = 1)\n    &quot;&quot;&quot;)\nfinally:\n    cursor.close()\n    conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0165","card":"q-database-with-python-126-warehouse-overload","sec":"database-with-python-s127","q":"Your app overloads a Snowflake warehouse and queries slow down. How do you fix it?","a":"<p>Scale the warehouse, tag queries for prioritization and tracking, split workloads into smaller queries, and monitor usage with built-in functions.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nfrom snowflake.connector import DictCursor\n\nconn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n    user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;, password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;, account=&#x27;your_account&#x27;,\n    warehouse=&#x27;your_warehouse&#x27;, database=&#x27;your_db&#x27;, schema=&#x27;your_schema&#x27;\n)\n\ntry:\n    cursor = conn.cursor(DictCursor)\n    cursor.execute(&quot;ALTER WAREHOUSE your_warehouse SET WAREHOUSE_SIZE = &#x27;LARGE&#x27;&quot;)\n    cursor.execute(&quot;ALTER SESSION SET QUERY_TAG = &#x27;high_priority_job&#x27;&quot;)\n\n    queries = [\n        &quot;SELECT * FROM large_table WHERE region = &#x27;A&#x27;&quot;,\n        &quot;SELECT * FROM large_table WHERE region = &#x27;B&#x27;&quot;\n    ]\n    for query in queries:\n        cursor.execute(query)\n        results = cursor.fetchall()\n        print(f&quot;Processed {len(results)} rows&quot;)\n\n    cursor.execute(&quot;SELECT * FROM TABLE(GET_WAREHOUSE_USAGE_HISTORY())&quot;)\n    print(cursor.fetchall())\nfinally:\n    cursor.close()\n    conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0166","card":"q-database-with-python-127-connection-dropped-mid-query","sec":"database-with-python-s128","q":"The connection drops during a long query. How do you handle it gracefully?","a":"<p>Retry with exponential backoff (the <code>tenacity</code> library), set connection timeouts and reconnect inside the retried function.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nfrom tenacity import retry, stop_after_attempt, wait_exponential, retry_if_exception_type\nfrom snowflake.connector.errors import OperationalError\n\nconn_params = {\n    &#x27;account&#x27;: &#x27;your_account&#x27;,\n    &#x27;user&#x27;: &#x27;your_user&#x27;,\n    &#x27;password&#x27;: &#x27;your_password&#x27;,\n    &#x27;database&#x27;: &#x27;your_database&#x27;,\n    &#x27;schema&#x27;: &#x27;your_schema&#x27;,\n    &#x27;warehouse&#x27;: &#x27;your_warehouse&#x27;,\n    &#x27;login_timeout&#x27;: 30\n}\n\n@retry(\n    stop=stop_after_attempt(3),\n    wait=wait_exponential(multiplier=1, min=4, max=10),\n    retry=retry_if_exception_type(OperationalError)\n)\ndef execute_query(query):\n    try:\n        conn = snowflake.connector.connect(**conn_params)\n        cursor = conn.cursor()\n        cursor.execute(query)\n        results = cursor.fetchall()\n        cursor.close()\n        conn.close()\n        return results\n    except OperationalError as e:\n        print(f&quot;Connection error: {e}. Retrying...&quot;)\n        raise   # re-raise so the decorator retries\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f&quot;Error: {e}&quot;)\n        raise\n\ntry:\n    print(execute_query(&quot;SELECT * FROM large_table&quot;))\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f&quot;Failed after retries: {e}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0167","card":"q-database-with-python-128-syntax-error-in-a-dynamic-query","sec":"database-with-python-s129","q":"A dynamically built query fails with a syntax error. How do you debug and prevent it?","a":"<p>Log the final query text with its parameters, use parameterized queries instead of string building, validate the SQL and test it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport logging\n\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.DEBUG, format=&#x27;%(asctime)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s&#x27;)\n\nconn_params = {\n    &#x27;account&#x27;: &#x27;your_account&#x27;,\n    &#x27;user&#x27;: &#x27;your_user&#x27;,\n    &#x27;password&#x27;: &#x27;your_password&#x27;,\n    &#x27;database&#x27;: &#x27;your_database&#x27;,\n    &#x27;schema&#x27;: &#x27;your_schema&#x27;\n}\n\ndef execute_safe_query(query, params=None):\n    try:\n        conn = snowflake.connector.connect(**conn_params)\n        cursor = conn.cursor()\n        logging.debug(f&quot;Executing query: {query} with params: {params}&quot;)\n        cursor.execute(query, params or ())\n        results = cursor.fetchall()\n        cursor.close()\n        conn.close()\n        return results\n    except snowflake.connector.errors.ProgrammingError as e:\n        logging.error(f&quot;Syntax error in query: {e}&quot;)\n        raise\n    except Exception as e:\n        logging.error(f&quot;Unexpected error: {e}&quot;)\n        raise\n\ntry:\n    query = &quot;SELECT * FROM employees WHERE department = %s AND salary &gt; %s&quot;\n    results = execute_safe_query(query, (&#x27;Engineering&#x27;, 50000))\n    print(results)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f&quot;Query failed: {e}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0168","card":"q-database-with-python-129-data-type-mismatch","sec":"database-with-python-s130","q":"An insert fails with a data type mismatch. How do you find and fix it?","a":"<p>Read the table schema (<code>DESCRIBE TABLE</code>), compare it with your values, cast inputs to the right type (Snowflake data type mapping) and read the error logs.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport logging\n\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO, format=&#x27;%(asctime)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s&#x27;)\n\nconn_params = {\n    &#x27;account&#x27;: &#x27;your_account&#x27;, &#x27;user&#x27;: &#x27;your_user&#x27;, &#x27;password&#x27;: &#x27;your_password&#x27;,\n    &#x27;database&#x27;: &#x27;your_database&#x27;, &#x27;schema&#x27;: &#x27;your_schema&#x27;\n}\n\ndef get_column_types(table_name):\n    conn = snowflake.connector.connect(**conn_params)\n    cursor = conn.cursor()\n    cursor.execute(f&quot;DESCRIBE TABLE {table_name}&quot;)\n    schema = {row[0]: row[1] for row in cursor.fetchall()}   # name -&gt; type\n    cursor.close()\n    conn.close()\n    return schema\n\ndef insert_data(table_name, data):\n    try:\n        schema = get_column_types(table_name)\n        logging.info(f&quot;Table schema: {schema}&quot;)\n\n        for row in data:\n            for key, value in row.items():\n                col_type = schema[key.upper()]\n                if &#x27;NUMBER&#x27; in col_type and isinstance(value, str):\n                    row[key] = int(float(value)) if value else None\n                elif &#x27;FLOAT&#x27; in col_type and isinstance(value, str):\n                    row[key] = float(value) if value else None\n\n        conn = snowflake.connector.connect(**conn_params)\n        cursor = conn.cursor()\n        columns = &#x27;, &#x27;.join(data[0].keys())\n        placeholders = &#x27;, &#x27;.join([&#x27;%s&#x27;] * len(data[0]))\n        query = f&quot;INSERT INTO {table_name} ({columns}) VALUES ({placeholders})&quot;\n        cursor.executemany(query, [list(row.values()) for row in data])\n        conn.commit()\n        cursor.close()\n        conn.close()\n        logging.info(&quot;Data inserted successfully&quot;)\n    except snowflake.connector.errors.ProgrammingError as e:\n        logging.error(f&quot;Data type mismatch: {e}&quot;)\n        raise\n\ndata = [\n    {&#x27;id&#x27;: &#x27;1&#x27;, &#x27;name&#x27;: &#x27;John&#x27;, &#x27;salary&#x27;: &#x27;50000.0&#x27;},\n    {&#x27;id&#x27;: &#x27;2&#x27;, &#x27;name&#x27;: &#x27;Jane&#x27;, &#x27;salary&#x27;: &#x27;60000.0&#x27;}\n]\ninsert_data(&#x27;employees&#x27;, data)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0169","card":"q-database-with-python-130-transaction-rollback","sec":"database-with-python-s131","q":"A script fails to roll back after an error. How do you manage transactions properly?","a":"<p>Turn off autocommit, run all statements, commit on success and roll back in the exception handler, then close the connection in <code>finally</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport logging\n\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO, format=&#x27;%(asctime)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s&#x27;)\n\nconn_params = {\n    &#x27;account&#x27;: &#x27;your_account&#x27;, &#x27;user&#x27;: &#x27;your_user&#x27;, &#x27;password&#x27;: &#x27;your_password&#x27;,\n    &#x27;database&#x27;: &#x27;your_database&#x27;, &#x27;schema&#x27;: &#x27;your_schema&#x27;\n}\n\ndef execute_transaction(queries):\n    conn = None\n    try:\n        conn = snowflake.connector.connect(**conn_params)\n        conn.autocommit(False)   # explicit transaction control\n        cursor = conn.cursor()\n        for query in queries:\n            logging.info(f&quot;Executing: {query}&quot;)\n            cursor.execute(query)\n        conn.commit()\n        logging.info(&quot;Transaction committed successfully&quot;)\n        cursor.close()\n    except Exception as e:\n        logging.error(f&quot;Transaction failed: {e}&quot;)\n        if conn:\n            conn.rollback()\n            logging.info(&quot;Transaction rolled back&quot;)\n        raise\n    finally:\n        if conn:\n            conn.close()\n\nqueries = [\n    &quot;INSERT INTO employees (id, name) VALUES (1, &#x27;John&#x27;)&quot;,\n    &quot;UPDATE employees SET salary = 50000 WHERE id = 1&quot;\n]\nexecute_transaction(queries)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0170","card":"q-database-with-python-131-deadlock-in-mysql","sec":"database-with-python-s132","q":"Concurrent updates cause a MySQL deadlock. How do you troubleshoot and prevent it?","a":"<p>Retry the transaction, keep a consistent query and lock order, keep transactions short, and use a suitable isolation level such as READ COMMITTED.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import pymysql\nfrom tenacity import retry, stop_after_attempt, wait_exponential, retry_if_exception_type\nimport logging\n\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO, format=&#x27;%(asctime)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s&#x27;)\n\nconn_params = {\n    &#x27;host&#x27;: &#x27;localhost&#x27;, &#x27;user&#x27;: &#x27;your_user&#x27;,\n    &#x27;password&#x27;: &#x27;your_password&#x27;, &#x27;database&#x27;: &#x27;your_database&#x27;\n}\n\n@retry(\n    stop=stop_after_attempt(3),\n    wait=wait_exponential(multiplier=1, min=2, max=5),\n    retry=retry_if_exception_type(pymysql.err.OperationalError)\n)\ndef execute_concurrent_update(query):\n    conn = None\n    try:\n        conn = pymysql.connect(**conn_params, charset=&#x27;utf8mb4&#x27;, cursorclass=pymysql.cursors.DictCursor)\n        conn.autocommit(False)\n        cursor = conn.cursor()\n        cursor.execute(&quot;SET TRANSACTION ISOLATION LEVEL READ COMMITTED&quot;)\n        logging.info(f&quot;Executing: {query}&quot;)\n        cursor.execute(query)\n        conn.commit()\n        cursor.close()\n        logging.info(&quot;Update successful&quot;)\n    except pymysql.err.OperationalError as e:\n        logging.error(f&quot;Deadlock detected: {e}&quot;)\n        if conn:\n            conn.rollback()\n        raise\n    except Exception as e:\n        logging.error(f&quot;Unexpected error: {e}&quot;)\n        if conn:\n            conn.rollback()\n        raise\n    finally:\n        if conn:\n            conn.close()\n\nexecute_concurrent_update(&quot;UPDATE employees SET salary = salary + 1000 WHERE id = 1&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0171","card":"q-database-with-python-132-time-travel-query-failure","sec":"database-with-python-s133","q":"A Time Travel query fails with \"Invalid timestamp\". How do you troubleshoot it?","a":"<p>Check the table's retention period, make sure the timestamp is within it, use the right timestamp format (UTC with <code>::TIMESTAMP_TZ</code>), and verify the <code>AT (TIMESTAMP =&gt; ...)</code> syntax.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nfrom datetime import datetime\nimport pytz\n\nconn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n    user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;, password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;, account=&#x27;your_account&#x27;,\n    warehouse=&#x27;your_warehouse&#x27;, database=&#x27;your_database&#x27;, schema=&#x27;your_schema&#x27;\n)\n\ntimestamp = datetime.now(pytz.UTC).strftime(&#x27;%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %Z&#x27;)\ntry:\n    cursor = conn.cursor()\n    cursor.execute(&quot;SHOW TABLES LIKE &#x27;your_table&#x27;&quot;)\n    retention_period = cursor.fetchone()[6]   # retention time in days\n    print(f&quot;Table retention period: {retention_period} days&quot;)\n\n    query = f&quot;&quot;&quot;\n    SELECT * FROM your_table\n    AT (TIMESTAMP =&gt; &#x27;{timestamp}&#x27;::TIMESTAMP_TZ)\n    &quot;&quot;&quot;\n    cursor.execute(query)\n    print(cursor.fetchall())\nexcept snowflake.connector.errors.ProgrammingError as e:\n    print(f&quot;Error: {e}&quot;)\n    print(&quot;Verify timestamp is within table&#x27;s retention period and format is correct.&quot;)\nfinally:\n    cursor.close()\n    conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0172","card":"q-database-with-python-133-moving-data-between-snowflake-and-postgr","sec":"database-with-python-s134","q":"How do you design and troubleshoot a Snowflake to PostgreSQL transfer?","a":"<p>Manage both connections, keep data types compatible (cast where needed), insert in a single PostgreSQL transaction (commit on success, roll back on error) and log type mismatches or connection issues.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport psycopg2\nimport pandas as pd\n\nsnow_conn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n    user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;, password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;, account=&#x27;your_account&#x27;,\n    warehouse=&#x27;your_warehouse&#x27;, database=&#x27;your_database&#x27;, schema=&#x27;your_schema&#x27;\n)\npg_conn = psycopg2.connect(\n    dbname=&#x27;your_db&#x27;, user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;, password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;,\n    host=&#x27;localhost&#x27;, port=&#x27;5432&#x27;\n)\n\ntry:\n    snow_cursor = snow_conn.cursor()\n    snow_cursor.execute(&quot;SELECT * FROM your_snowflake_table&quot;)\n    snow_data = pd.DataFrame(snow_cursor.fetchall(), columns=[desc[0] for desc in snow_cursor.description])\n    snow_data = snow_data.astype(str)   # avoid type mismatches\n\n    pg_cursor = pg_conn.cursor()\n    for _, row in snow_data.iterrows():\n        pg_cursor.execute(\n            &quot;INSERT INTO your_pg_table (column1, column2) VALUES (%s, %s)&quot;,\n            (row[&#x27;COLUMN1&#x27;], row[&#x27;COLUMN2&#x27;])\n        )\n    pg_conn.commit()\nexcept Exception as e:\n    pg_conn.rollback()\n    print(f&quot;Error: {e}&quot;)\nfinally:\n    snow_cursor.close()\n    pg_conn.close()\n    snow_conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0173","card":"q-database-with-python-134-special-characters-and-emojis","sec":"database-with-python-s135","q":"Inserting emojis or special characters fails. How do you resolve it?","a":"<p>Use UTF-8 end to end: Python stdout and string encoding, Snowflake string handling and the table collation. Always pass values as bind parameters.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport sys\n\nsys.stdout.reconfigure(encoding=&#x27;utf-8&#x27;)\n\nconn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n    user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;, password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;, account=&#x27;your_account&#x27;,\n    warehouse=&#x27;your_warehouse&#x27;, database=&#x27;your_database&#x27;, schema=&#x27;your_schema&#x27;\n)\n\ntry:\n    cursor = conn.cursor()\n    cursor.execute(&quot;CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE test_table (data VARCHAR(100)) COLLATE &#x27;utf8&#x27;&quot;)\n    special_data = &quot;Hello 😊 World&quot;\n    cursor.execute(\n        &quot;INSERT INTO test_table (data) VALUES (%s)&quot;,\n        (special_data.encode(&#x27;utf-8&#x27;).decode(&#x27;utf-8&#x27;),)\n    )\n    conn.commit()\n    print(&quot;Data inserted successfully&quot;)\nexcept snowflake.connector.errors.ProgrammingError as e:\n    print(f&quot;Error: {e}&quot;)   # check table collation and Python encoding are UTF-8\nfinally:\n    cursor.close()\n    conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0174","card":"q-database-with-python-135-dynamic-schema-switching","sec":"database-with-python-s136","q":"How do you switch Snowflake schemas at runtime and troubleshoot it?","a":"<p>Run <code>USE SCHEMA</code>, confirm with <code>CURRENT_SCHEMA()</code>, handle errors, and check that the schema exists and you have permission (<code>SHOW SCHEMAS</code>).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\n\nconn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n    user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;, password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;, account=&#x27;your_account&#x27;,\n    warehouse=&#x27;your_warehouse&#x27;, database=&#x27;your_database&#x27;\n)\n\nschemas = [&#x27;schema1&#x27;, &#x27;schema2&#x27;]\ntry:\n    cursor = conn.cursor()\n    for schema in schemas:\n        cursor.execute(f&quot;USE SCHEMA {schema}&quot;)\n        cursor.execute(&quot;SELECT CURRENT_SCHEMA()&quot;)\n        print(f&quot;Switched to schema: {cursor.fetchone()[0]}&quot;)\n        cursor.execute(&quot;SELECT * FROM your_table LIMIT 1&quot;)\n        print(cursor.fetchall())\nexcept snowflake.connector.errors.ProgrammingError as e:\n    print(f&quot;Error: {e}&quot;)\n    cursor.execute(&quot;SHOW SCHEMAS&quot;)\n    print([row[1] for row in cursor.fetchall()])\nfinally:\n    cursor.close()\n    conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0175","card":"q-database-with-python-136-stage-file-upload-failure","sec":"database-with-python-s137","q":"Uploading a file to a Snowflake stage fails. What do you check?","a":"<p>Stage configuration and permissions, the file format, that the file exists locally, and the upload method (<code>PUT</code>). Verify with <code>LIST @stage</code> and <code>SHOW STAGES</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport os\n\nconn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n    user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;, password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;, account=&#x27;your_account&#x27;,\n    warehouse=&#x27;your_warehouse&#x27;, database=&#x27;your_database&#x27;, schema=&#x27;your_schema&#x27;\n)\n\ntry:\n    cursor = conn.cursor()\n    cursor.execute(&quot;CREATE OR REPLACE STAGE my_stage FILE_FORMAT = (TYPE = CSV)&quot;)\n\n    file_path = &quot;data.csv&quot;\n    if not os.path.exists(file_path):\n        raise FileNotFoundError(&quot;File not found&quot;)\n\n    cursor.execute(f&quot;PUT file://{file_path} @my_stage AUTO_COMPRESS = TRUE&quot;)\n    print(&quot;File uploaded successfully&quot;)\n    cursor.execute(&quot;LIST @my_stage&quot;)\n    print(cursor.fetchall())\nexcept snowflake.connector.errors.ProgrammingError as e:\n    print(f&quot;Error: {e}&quot;)\n    cursor.execute(&quot;SHOW STAGES&quot;)\n    print(cursor.fetchall())\nfinally:\n    cursor.close()\n    conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0176","card":"q-database-with-python-137-concurrent-connections-overload","sec":"database-with-python-s138","q":"Many scripts exceed the Snowflake connection limit. How do you mitigate it?","a":"<p>Pool connections (SQLAlchemy <code>pool_size</code> and <code>max_overflow</code>), limit concurrency, review the account settings and balance load across scripts. Call <code>engine.dispose()</code> to clean up.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from sqlalchemy import create_engine\nfrom urllib.parse import quote_plus\n\nsnowflake_url = (\n    f&quot;snowflake://your_user:{quote_plus(&#x27;your_password&#x27;)}@your_account/&quot;\n    f&quot;your_database/your_schema?warehouse=your_warehouse&quot;\n)\nengine = create_engine(snowflake_url, pool_size=5, max_overflow=10)\n\ntry:\n    with engine.connect() as conn:\n        result = conn.execute(&quot;SELECT CURRENT_WAREHOUSE(), CURRENT_DATABASE()&quot;)\n        print(result.fetchall())\n        conn.execute(&quot;SELECT * FROM your_table LIMIT 1&quot;)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f&quot;Error: {e}&quot;)   # check Snowflake account connection limits\nfinally:\n    engine.dispose()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0177","card":"q-database-with-python-138-cross-region-connection","sec":"database-with-python-s139","q":"A script in one cloud region cannot reach a Snowflake instance in another region. How do you resolve it?","a":"<p>Use the region-specific account URL, and check cross-region replication, network latency and DNS configuration. <code>CURRENT_REGION()</code> confirms where you connected.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\n\nconn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n    user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;,\n    password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;,\n    account=&#x27;your_account.us-west-2&#x27;,   # specify region\n    warehouse=&#x27;your_warehouse&#x27;,\n    database=&#x27;your_database&#x27;,\n    schema=&#x27;your_schema&#x27;\n)\n\ntry:\n    cursor = conn.cursor()\n    cursor.execute(&quot;SELECT CURRENT_REGION()&quot;)\n    print(f&quot;Connected to region: {cursor.fetchone()[0]}&quot;)\n    cursor.execute(&quot;SELECT * FROM your_table LIMIT 1&quot;)\n    print(cursor.fetchall())\nexcept snowflake.connector.errors.OperationalError as e:\n    print(f&quot;Error: {e}&quot;)\n    print(&quot;Verify account URL and network connectivity&quot;)\nfinally:\n    cursor.close()\n    conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0178","card":"q-database-with-python-139-null-handling","sec":"database-with-python-s140","q":"A script misreads NULL values from Snowflake. How do you handle them?","a":"<p>NULL arrives as Python <code>None</code>. Check for <code>None</code>, use default values (<code>fillna</code> in pandas) and review the query logic.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport pandas as pd\n\nconn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n    user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;, password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;, account=&#x27;your_account&#x27;,\n    warehouse=&#x27;your_warehouse&#x27;, database=&#x27;your_database&#x27;, schema=&#x27;your_schema&#x27;\n)\n\ntry:\n    cursor = conn.cursor()\n    cursor.execute(&quot;SELECT column1, column2 FROM your_table&quot;)\n    df = pd.DataFrame(cursor.fetchall(), columns=[desc[0] for desc in cursor.description])\n\n    df.fillna({&#x27;column1&#x27;: &#x27;default_value&#x27;, &#x27;column2&#x27;: 0}, inplace=True)\n    for index, row in df.iterrows():\n        column1 = row[&#x27;column1&#x27;] if row[&#x27;column1&#x27;] is not None else &#x27;default_value&#x27;\n        column2 = row[&#x27;column2&#x27;] if row[&#x27;column2&#x27;] is not None else 0\n        print(f&quot;Row {index}: {column1}, {column2}&quot;)\nexcept snowflake.connector.errors.ProgrammingError as e:\n    print(f&quot;Error: {e}&quot;)\nfinally:\n    cursor.close()\n    conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0179","card":"q-database-with-python-140-query-tags-not-showing-in-history","sec":"database-with-python-s141","q":"Query tags set for cost tracking do not appear in query history. How do you debug it?","a":"<p>Set the tag with <code>ALTER SESSION SET QUERY_TAG</code>, run the query, check the tag in <code>INFORMATION_SCHEMA.QUERY_HISTORY()</code>, and review session parameters (<code>SHOW PARAMETERS LIKE 'QUERY_TAG'</code>), tag visibility and permissions.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\n\nconn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n    user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;, password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;, account=&#x27;your_account&#x27;,\n    warehouse=&#x27;your_warehouse&#x27;, database=&#x27;your_database&#x27;, schema=&#x27;your_schema&#x27;\n)\n\ntry:\n    cursor = conn.cursor()\n    cursor.execute(&quot;ALTER SESSION SET QUERY_TAG = &#x27;cost_tracking_tag&#x27;&quot;)\n    cursor.execute(&quot;SELECT * FROM your_table LIMIT 1&quot;)\n    print(cursor.fetchall())\n\n    cursor.execute(&quot;SELECT * FROM TABLE(INFORMATION_SCHEMA.QUERY_HISTORY()) WHERE QUERY_TAG = &#x27;cost_tracking_tag&#x27;&quot;)\n    print(cursor.fetchall())\nexcept snowflake.connector.errors.ProgrammingError as e:\n    print(f&quot;Error: {e}&quot;)\n    cursor.execute(&quot;SHOW PARAMETERS LIKE &#x27;QUERY_TAG&#x27;&quot;)\n    print(cursor.fetchall())\nfinally:\n    cursor.close()\n    conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0180","card":"q-database-with-python-141-legacy-driver-conflict","sec":"database-with-python-s142","q":"An old MySQL driver conflicts with the newer Snowflake connector. How do you resolve it?","a":"<p>Isolate the app in a virtual environment, pin compatible driver versions with <code>pip</code>, and verify with <code>pip list</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>python -m venv snowflake_env\nsource snowflake_env/bin/activate        # Windows: snowflake_env\\Scripts\\activate\npip install snowflake-connector-python==2.9.0 mysql-connector-python==8.0.33\npip list</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport mysql.connector\n\nsnow_conn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n    user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;, password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;, account=&#x27;your_account&#x27;,\n    warehouse=&#x27;your_warehouse&#x27;, database=&#x27;your_database&#x27;, schema=&#x27;your_schema&#x27;\n)\nmysql_conn = mysql.connector.connect(\n    host=&#x27;localhost&#x27;, user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;, password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;, database=&#x27;your_db&#x27;\n)\n\ntry:\n    snow_cursor = snow_conn.cursor()\n    snow_cursor.execute(&quot;SELECT * FROM your_table LIMIT 1&quot;)\n    print(snow_cursor.fetchall())\n\n    mysql_cursor = mysql_conn.cursor()\n    mysql_cursor.execute(&quot;SELECT * FROM your_mysql_table LIMIT 1&quot;)\n    print(mysql_cursor.fetchall())\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f&quot;Error: {e}&quot;)\nfinally:\n    snow_cursor.close()\n    mysql_cursor.close()\n    snow_conn.close()\n    mysql_conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0181","card":"q-database-with-python-142-snowflake-stream-not-detecting-changes","sec":"database-with-python-s143","q":"A script monitoring a Snowflake stream for change data capture sees no new data. What could be wrong?","a":"<p>Stream configuration, change tracking on the table, the polling logic and the stream retention period. Check with <code>SHOW STREAMS</code> and <code>SHOW TABLES</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport time\n\nconn = snowflake.connector.connect(\n    user=&#x27;your_user&#x27;, password=&#x27;your_password&#x27;, account=&#x27;your_account&#x27;,\n    warehouse=&#x27;your_warehouse&#x27;, database=&#x27;your_database&#x27;, schema=&#x27;your_schema&#x27;\n)\n\ntry:\n    cursor = conn.cursor()\n    cursor.execute(&quot;CREATE OR REPLACE STREAM my_stream ON TABLE your_table&quot;)\n\n    while True:\n        cursor.execute(&quot;SELECT * FROM my_stream&quot;)\n        changes = cursor.fetchall()\n        if changes:\n            print(f&quot;New changes detected: {changes}&quot;)\n        else:\n            print(&quot;No new changes&quot;)\n        time.sleep(60)   # poll every minute\n\n        cursor.execute(&quot;SHOW STREAMS LIKE &#x27;my_stream&#x27;&quot;)\n        print(f&quot;Stream retention: {cursor.fetchone()}&quot;)\nexcept snowflake.connector.errors.ProgrammingError as e:\n    print(f&quot;Error: {e}&quot;)\n    cursor.execute(&quot;SHOW TABLES LIKE &#x27;your_table&#x27;&quot;)\n    print(cursor.fetchall())\nfinally:\n    cursor.close()\n    conn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0182","card":"q-database-with-python-143-connection-leak-in-a-long-running-app","sec":"database-with-python-s144","q":"A long-running app leaks Snowflake connections. How do you detect and prevent it?","a":"<p>Wrap connections in a context manager that always closes them, monitor open resources (for example with <code>psutil</code>) and stop when a threshold is exceeded.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nfrom contextlib import contextmanager\nimport logging\nimport psutil\nimport os\n\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n@contextmanager\ndef snowflake_connection(config):\n    conn = None\n    try:\n        conn = snowflake.connector.connect(**config)\n        yield conn\n    except Exception as e:\n        logger.error(f&quot;Connection error: {e}&quot;)\n        raise\n    finally:\n        if conn:\n            conn.close()\n            logger.info(&quot;Connection closed&quot;)\n\ndef monitor_connections():\n    process = psutil.Process(os.getpid())\n    open_files = process.open_files()\n    logger.info(f&quot;Open file descriptors: {len(open_files)}&quot;)\n    return len(open_files)\n\nconfig = {\n    &#x27;user&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_USER&#x27;),\n    &#x27;password&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_PASSWORD&#x27;),\n    &#x27;account&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_ACCOUNT&#x27;),\n    &#x27;warehouse&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_WAREHOUSE&#x27;),\n    &#x27;database&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_DATABASE&#x27;),\n    &#x27;schema&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_SCHEMA&#x27;)\n}\n\nif monitor_connections() &gt; 50:   # threshold\n    logger.warning(&quot;Too many open connections, aborting&quot;)\n    raise ResourceWarning(&quot;Connection limit exceeded&quot;)\n\nwith snowflake_connection(config) as conn:\n    cursor = conn.cursor()\n    cursor.execute(&quot;SELECT CURRENT_VERSION()&quot;)\n    logger.info(f&quot;Snowflake version: {cursor.fetchone()[0]}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0183","card":"q-database-with-python-144-monitoring-query-performance","sec":"database-with-python-s145","q":"How do you log and monitor Snowflake query performance and errors from Python?","a":"<p>Log to a file and the console, time every query, tag the session, log failures with elapsed time, and send an alert (email or Slack) on error. Snowflake's query history gives server-side metrics.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport logging\nimport time\nimport os\n\nlogging.basicConfig(\n    level=logging.INFO,\n    format=&#x27;%(asctime)s - %(levelname)s - %(message)s&#x27;,\n    handlers=[logging.FileHandler(&#x27;query_performance.log&#x27;), logging.StreamHandler()]\n)\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\ndef send_alert(message):\n    logger.warning(f&quot;Alert: {message}&quot;)   # integrate Slack or email here\n\ndef execute_query_with_monitoring(conn, query):\n    start_time = time.time()\n    try:\n        cursor = conn.cursor()\n        cursor.execute(&quot;ALTER SESSION SET QUERY_TAG = &#x27;performance_monitoring&#x27;&quot;)\n        cursor.execute(query)\n        results = cursor.fetchall()\n        logger.info(f&quot;Query executed successfully: {query[:50]}... Time: {time.time() - start_time:.2f}s&quot;)\n        return results\n    except Exception as e:\n        logger.error(f&quot;Query failed: {query[:50]}... Error: {e}, Time: {time.time() - start_time:.2f}s&quot;)\n        send_alert(f&quot;Query error: {e}&quot;)\n        raise\n\nconfig = {\n    &#x27;user&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_USER&#x27;),\n    &#x27;password&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_PASSWORD&#x27;),\n    &#x27;account&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_ACCOUNT&#x27;),\n    &#x27;warehouse&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_WAREHOUSE&#x27;),\n    &#x27;database&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_DATABASE&#x27;),\n    &#x27;schema&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_SCHEMA&#x27;)\n}\nconn = snowflake.connector.connect(**config)\nresults = execute_query_with_monitoring(conn, &quot;SELECT * FROM my_table WHERE date &gt; &#x27;2023-01-01&#x27;&quot;)\nconn.close()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0184","card":"q-database-with-python-145-scheduled-maintenance-window","sec":"database-with-python-s146","q":"A script fails during a Snowflake maintenance window. How do you handle interruptions?","a":"<p>Retry with exponential backoff, know the maintenance schedule, and fail over by delaying execution or switching to a backup process.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport time\nimport logging\nimport os\nfrom retrying import retry\n\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\n@retry(\n    stop_max_attempt_number=3,\n    wait_exponential_multiplier=1000,\n    wait_exponential_max=10000,\n    retry_on_exception=lambda e: isinstance(e, snowflake.connector.errors.OperationalError)\n)\ndef execute_query_with_retry(conn, query):\n    cursor = conn.cursor()\n    cursor.execute(query)\n    return cursor.fetchall()\n\ndef run_query_with_maintenance_handling(config, query):\n    try:\n        conn = snowflake.connector.connect(**config)\n        results = execute_query_with_retry(conn, query)\n        logger.info(f&quot;Query executed successfully: {query[:50]}...&quot;)\n        return results\n    except snowflake.connector.errors.OperationalError as e:\n        logger.error(f&quot;Maintenance window likely in progress: {e}&quot;)\n        logger.info(&quot;Switching to failover: delaying execution&quot;)\n        time.sleep(3600)   # wait for maintenance to complete\n        conn = snowflake.connector.connect(**config)\n        return execute_query_with_retry(conn, query)\n    finally:\n        if &#x27;conn&#x27; in locals():\n            conn.close()\n\nconfig = {\n    &#x27;user&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_USER&#x27;),\n    &#x27;password&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_PASSWORD&#x27;),\n    &#x27;account&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_ACCOUNT&#x27;),\n    &#x27;warehouse&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_WAREHOUSE&#x27;),\n    &#x27;database&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_DATABASE&#x27;),\n    &#x27;schema&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_SCHEMA&#x27;)\n}\nresults = run_query_with_maintenance_handling(config, &quot;SELECT * FROM my_table&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0185","card":"q-database-with-python-146-compatibility-after-a-version-upgrade","sec":"database-with-python-s147","q":"A script breaks after a Snowflake version upgrade. How do you identify and fix it?","a":"<p>Read the release notes, check <code>CURRENT_VERSION()</code>, upgrade <code>snowflake-connector-python</code>, and test in a staging environment first.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport logging\nimport subprocess\nimport os\n\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\ndef check_snowflake_version(conn):\n    cursor = conn.cursor()\n    cursor.execute(&quot;SELECT CURRENT_VERSION()&quot;)\n    version = cursor.fetchone()[0]\n    logger.info(f&quot;Current Snowflake version: {version}&quot;)\n    return version\n\ndef update_snowflake_connector():\n    try:\n        subprocess.check_call([&#x27;pip&#x27;, &#x27;install&#x27;, &#x27;--upgrade&#x27;, &#x27;snowflake-connector-python&#x27;])\n        logger.info(&quot;Snowflake connector updated successfully&quot;)\n    except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n        logger.error(f&quot;Failed to update snowflake-connector-python: {e}&quot;)\n        raise\n\ndef test_connection(config):\n    try:\n        conn = snowflake.connector.connect(**config)\n        check_snowflake_version(conn)\n        conn.cursor().execute(&quot;SELECT * FROM my_table LIMIT 1&quot;)\n        logger.info(&quot;Test query executed successfully&quot;)\n        conn.close()\n    except Exception as e:\n        logger.error(f&quot;Compatibility issue detected: {e}&quot;)\n        update_snowflake_connector()\n        conn = snowflake.connector.connect(**config)\n        conn.cursor().execute(&quot;SELECT * FROM my_table LIMIT 1&quot;)\n        logger.info(&quot;Test query executed successfully after update&quot;)\n        conn.close()\n\nconfig = {\n    &#x27;user&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_USER&#x27;),\n    &#x27;password&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_PASSWORD&#x27;),\n    &#x27;account&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_ACCOUNT&#x27;),\n    &#x27;warehouse&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_WAREHOUSE&#x27;),\n    &#x27;database&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_DATABASE&#x27;),\n    &#x27;schema&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_SCHEMA&#x27;)\n}\ntest_connection(config)   # run in staging first</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"database-with-python-f0186","card":"q-database-with-python-147-automated-credential-rotation","sec":"database-with-python-s148","q":"Credentials must be rotated periodically. How do you automate it?","a":"<p>Keep secrets in a secret manager (AWS Secrets Manager), fetch the new credentials, test them with a connection, and fall back to the old credentials on failure. Run the job on a schedule (AWS Lambda or cron).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import snowflake.connector\nimport boto3\nimport json\nimport logging\nimport os\n\nlogging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO)\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\ndef get_new_credentials(secret_id):\n    client = boto3.client(&#x27;secretsmanager&#x27;)\n    response = client.get_secret_value(SecretId=secret_id)\n    return json.loads(response[&#x27;SecretString&#x27;])\n\ndef rotate_credentials(secret_id, config):\n    try:\n        new_creds = get_new_credentials(secret_id)\n        config[&#x27;user&#x27;] = new_creds[&#x27;user&#x27;]\n        config[&#x27;password&#x27;] = new_creds[&#x27;password&#x27;]\n        logger.info(&quot;Credentials rotated successfully&quot;)\n\n        conn = snowflake.connector.connect(**config)\n        cursor = conn.cursor()\n        cursor.execute(&quot;SELECT CURRENT_VERSION()&quot;)\n        logger.info(&quot;Connection test successful with new credentials&quot;)\n        conn.close()\n        return config\n    except Exception as e:\n        logger.error(f&quot;Credential rotation failed: {e}&quot;)\n        raise   # roll back to previous credentials or fail over\n\nconfig = {\n    &#x27;user&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_USER&#x27;),\n    &#x27;password&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_PASSWORD&#x27;),\n    &#x27;account&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_ACCOUNT&#x27;),\n    &#x27;warehouse&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_WAREHOUSE&#x27;),\n    &#x27;database&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_DATABASE&#x27;),\n    &#x27;schema&#x27;: os.getenv(&#x27;SNOWFLAKE_SCHEMA&#x27;)\n}\nupdated_config = rotate_credentials(&#x27;snowflake/credentials&#x27;, config)</code></pre></div>","hand":false}];
